1
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:21,448
Visit turkision.com for more!

2
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:28,079
Come on. We are just starting.

3
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:36,479
Come on, jackals!

4
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:38,959
I am still alive!

5
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:52,319
Alps! Everyone to horses!

6
00:02:52,399 --> 00:02:53,399
Cukurdibi.

7
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:56,439
It happened at Cukurdibi.

8
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,999
Osman. My Allah, protect him.

9
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,399
-Come on.
-Come on!

10
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:20,559
Yakup Bey.

11
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,919
Come on.

12
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,639
Boran!

13
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,239
We will go this way.

14
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:50,199
-There alps coming from the tribe.
-Come on Yakup Bey, there is no time.

15
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:57,919
You answer goodness with illness!

16
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:00,639
Where do you think you are running to?

17
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:05,599
Their arrogance made them blind! We
will make them right with our swords!

18
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:07,599
Attack, alps!

19
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:16,839
Don’t you know those who lay eyes
upon my land dies!

20
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:59,839
Ambush!

21
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,359
Be cautious!

22
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:19,199
Whoever did this knew we were coming!

23
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:25,319
You don't know who you are messing with!

24
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:31,079
The Righteous!

25
00:05:55,840 --> 00:06:00,079
Come on alps! My father waits us!

26
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:46,639
-Konur!
-Yakup Bey!

27
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:50,399
Stop!

28
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:54,839
Konur is with us.

29
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:10,559
Come on, let us leave before alps arrive.

30
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:18,039
Osman.

31
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:28,359
So you are still alive.

32
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:31,439
I will take your life myself.

33
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:33,239
Why?

34
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:38,039
Why are you
still standing? This is th,e time, come on!

35
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:42,879
Ibrahim Bey! Melike Hatun!

36
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,359
This is not the time.

37
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:47,439
The reinforcements from the tribe should
be on its way.

38
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:50,239
Come on.

39
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:52,079
Ibrahim Bey!

40
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:54,079
I said, come on.

41
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:47,439
Boran!

42
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:01,599
Boran.

43
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:12,719
Boran!

44
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,839
Konur!

45
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:31,599
Konur!

46
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:37,879
Boran!

47
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:42,079
What are you up to!

48
00:09:42,680 --> 00:09:44,399
Forgive me, my Bey.

49
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:46,919
We didn't foresee this happening.

50
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:49,479
Forgive us.

51
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:57,079
My Bey!

52
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:58,959
Osman!

53
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,039
My Bey.

54
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:04,159
-Are you alright?
-I am alright.

55
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:07,999
They ran off.

56
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:16,039
-Osman, are you alright?
-I am alright.

57
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:24,519
Even the devil would envy what they’ve done.

58
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:28,639
They placed the fires night before.

59
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:30,639
We couldn't have known.

60
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:35,079
They betrayed us, my Bey. To hell with their lives.

61
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:39,119
We couldn't have known Boran would do this.

62
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:43,279
A traitor wouldn't lock the door now would he?

63
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:49,119
What about Konur?
Did he have something to do with this?

64
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:51,359
Konur went after them as well.

65
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:54,439
We will learn their intentions.

66
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:59,679
However, what they've done here was the last straw.

67
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:04,639
-What will we do now, my Bey?
-We will not let them get away with this.

68
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:07,759
Of course we will make them pay.

69
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:12,839
Of course we will. Come on, let us move.

70
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:22,839
Germiyanoglu Border - Frontier Market

71
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:40,359
Thank Allah, you came back well, father.

72
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,879
Did you send word to Beys, Mehmed?

73
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:45,559
All the Beys have answered our call for war.

74
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,919
They will be here soon.

75
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:51,559
Good.

76
00:11:56,480 --> 00:12:00,079
There are a lot of men to be teached at frontiers.

77
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:02,079
And how will we teach them, father?

78
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:04,159
With those?

79
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:11,359
Mehmed.

80
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:15,239
This is not the time to be seperated.

81
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:18,039
But to be united.

82
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:23,879
They released us from the captivity of Osman.

83
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:28,519
Do not forget that.

84
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:38,559
Ulcay and Tugay will watch them closely.

85
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:44,719
Their heads will roll with a single mistake.

86
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,599
Let the judge come..

87
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,999
..and justice be secured first.

88
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:57,559
Their fate will be dealt with later.

89
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:02,439
Mehmed. Are there any news from Alaeddin?

90
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:06,159
All villages and caves were
checked at southern and northern region.

91
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:09,359
However, they are still missing.

92
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:12,439
Now it is time for houses and caves..

93
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:14,999
..at the Dimbos region.

94
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,439
I will go there.

95
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:18,439
Tell Ulcay.

96
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:21,119
Let him come with you.

97
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:23,839
Search thoroughly together.

98
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,959
Ruknettin, the judge...

99
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:29,679
...is a great scholar.

100
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:33,519
I've heard his fame numerous times.

101
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:40,599
However, it is a pity I
will see his face in dark days like these.

102
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:43,599
It is.

103
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:46,399
We haven't seen him as well.

104
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,599
A great judge is coming..

105
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:52,879
..and we still can not find Alaeddin.

106
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:57,439
Come on, Mehmed.

107
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:02,599
Dogan, tell Ulcay.

108
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:13,119
Dogan, tell that
jackal, we will search from both sides.

109
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,759
Even his scent makes me nauseous.

110
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:27,519
Yakup Bey.

111
00:14:28,680 --> 00:14:30,879
This search..

112
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:35,319
..is finding a needle in a hay bale.

113
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:39,959
There are many gutters at frontiers.

114
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:46,319
We need information from Osman.

115
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:50,079
Konur! Boran

116
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:52,679
Come on.

117
00:14:56,880 --> 00:15:00,599
Yes, Ibrahim Bey.

118
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:05,239
You know everything about Osman.

119
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:09,279
Find where..

120
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:13,279
..Alaeddin is.

121
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:19,879
We are watching Osman and his tribe
for two days as per UIcay's request.

122
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:22,479
We know their every move.

123
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:26,799
We will give you
the right information to find Alaeddin.

124
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,799
Thank you.

125
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:39,519
I suppose there is
no harm searching for him from four sides.

126
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:44,919
Come now. Tell us.

127
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:02,519
Be well, my Bey.

128
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,839
-Thank Allah.
-Are you alright, my Bey?

129
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:09,759
-My Bey, are you alright?
-Thank Allah, we are alright. Do not worry.

130
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:13,239
-Thank Allah, we are alright.
-May you live long, my Bey.

131
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:17,359
May Allah protect you, my Bey.

132
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:21,479
What is it?

133
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:24,079
What is this?

134
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,759
Listen.

135
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:37,799
How could you have known?

136
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:39,639
Don't get your heads down.

137
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:41,879
Don't. Do not.

138
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:46,119
How could you have known that they'd
bury their children and attempt to run off?

139
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:51,439
How could you have
known that they'd set fires and traps?

140
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:56,479
This seems to be a game of Ulcay's.

141
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:59,559
What makes you think so, Osman Bey?

142
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:01,759
It may Ibrahim and Yakup too.

143
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:03,599
No.

144
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:07,638
I never believe our people can be this vile.

145
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:12,999
They want to make brothers fight each other.

146
00:17:13,839 --> 00:17:18,279
Our people would never go this far.

147
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,878
If we do what they want,

148
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:24,999
..too much blood will be shed.

149
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:29,879
Too many heads will fall.

150
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:35,319
But we will prevent this...

151
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:38,919
...as much as we can and our morals allow us.

152
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:43,839
Didn't they violate the morals long ago, Osman Bey?

153
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:48,039
Losing a child, Gunduz Bey...

154
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:52,039
We all know what it does to a person...

155
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:55,119
...and what it can make people do.

156
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:58,319
Losing a child...

157
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:01,919
It's such poison that...

158
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,999
...it may be a great trouble...

159
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,719
...if it flows in the wrong vein.

160
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,559
But we..

161
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:19,879
...will never let this trouble rise.

162
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:26,199
Come on. I expect to see everyone in my tent.

163
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:32,479
Even if one of Kayis is excluded from the tribe

164
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:34,519
...they never lose contact.

165
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:36,639
They always keep in touch.

166
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,919
Thanks to this,
we know all the secret ways they use.

167
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:41,199
Ha, Boran?

168
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:44,159
For sure, we know them all.

169
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:47,919
If there aren't some they keep secret from us.

170
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:52,439
Well..

171
00:18:52,520 --> 00:18:56,319
Yakup Bey must see your usefulness...

172
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:59,519
...so he can stop doubting.

173
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:09,239
Whatever is needed
will be done without hesitation, my Bey.

174
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:22,279
Now..

175
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:28,399
Let's see who can save Osman from us, Yakup Bey.

176
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,319
It's been obvious Osman will be destroyed...

177
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:37,759
..due to what he has done so far.

178
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:42,799
His end was just waiting for a reason.

179
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:47,599
He caused our children to die.

180
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:53,639
Only death is waiting for Osman now.

181
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,519
Whoever killed Ahmed

182
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:03,239
...they would never let the judge...

183
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:05,559
...secure the justice in these lands.

184
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:09,319
Justice is the
last thing they'd desire in these lands.

185
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:12,439
Yes. Yes.

186
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:18,639
Well... Judge is coming from Karesi.

187
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:21,319
And he's going to spend the night in the inn.

188
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:24,079
-Orhan.
-My Bey.

189
00:20:25,280 --> 00:20:27,399
Elcim.

190
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:32,679
You go visit the judge.

191
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:35,999
And make him reach this land safely.

192
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:39,639
You should be
disguised. Don't let anyone notice you.

193
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:41,879
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

194
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:44,759
Go now.

195
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:49,399
Well..

196
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:53,519
Alaaddin...

197
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:56,439
Send Hasan to Alaaddin.

198
00:20:56,560 --> 00:21:00,759
We can't let anyone see him until the trial.

199
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:03,279
As you order, my Bey.

200
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:09,439
Gunduz Bey.

201
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:11,879
Let's talk about the conquest of Mekece.

202
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:14,559
In such time?
-Well...

203
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:17,959
No times can keep us away from the conquests.

204
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:21,639
We'd perform
the conquest even if we're deep in blood.

205
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:26,039
Now... Ibrahim Bey and Yakup Bey...

206
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:29,479
...are bringing
their armies not only for our lands...

207
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:32,759
...but also for the conquest of Mekece.

208
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:35,519
We need to act quickly.

209
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:41,639
For this reason, start
sending your alps for the conquest already.

210
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,999
Whatever you wish, Osman Bey.

211
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:57,639
Where are you?

212
00:21:58,160 --> 00:22:00,199
Jackal!

213
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:03,439
Are you in your nest?

214
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:12,599
Melike Sultan...

215
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:15,519
You invited me.

216
00:22:15,800 --> 00:22:19,399
So I got out of my nest and came here.

217
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:22,599
Make your wish now.

218
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:25,999
Kill Judge Rukneddin.

219
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:30,879
Our servant Kamil will take his place.

220
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:33,079
I've sent him a message.

221
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:36,199
He's going to hit the road soon.

222
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:42,359
Why would you want to kill the judge?

223
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:45,919
We know Alaaddin killed my son.

224
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:49,799
But the judge is going to demand witnesses...

225
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:52,479
...and investigate elaborately.

226
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:54,199
And this will make it longer.

227
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:57,719
Osman will try
to distract the judge in the meantime.

228
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,919
You're not leaving it to chance, huh?

229
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:05,479
Fine.

230
00:23:07,080 --> 00:23:13,119
What will you do when
Osman realizes that we killed the judge?

231
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:17,319
Alaaddin will be dead by that time.

232
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:21,039
So it won't matter.

233
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:23,879
Be careful, though.

234
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:26,599
Nobody should know the judge is dead...

235
00:23:26,760 --> 00:23:30,039
..until the trial is over.

236
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:34,679
The judge will be dead.

237
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:50,759
I don't know..

238
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:54,039
...if the devil
is needed while there is this woman.

239
00:23:54,320 --> 00:23:56,959
No devils can be better than you, Ulcay.

240
00:23:57,200 --> 00:24:00,879
You yourself killed
the child of the woman who you call devil.

241
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:07,199
There's always someone greater.

242
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:15,559
Let's go kill the judge.

243
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:20,319
This is the place where I last saw Gonca.

244
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:22,679
The way splits into two here.

245
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:24,999
-Gokmen.
-My Shahzade.

246
00:24:25,120 --> 00:24:28,639
You go north
with the alps who are coming from behind.

247
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:34,319
Kanyumaz and I will go south.

248
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:37,439
Gokmen.

249
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:42,359
Nobody will go back to the
tribe before finding Alaaddin and Gonca.

250
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:44,199
As you order, my Shahzade.

251
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:47,279
Kill Alaaddin wherever you see him.

252
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:52,119
My Shahzade, what about Gonca Hatun?

253
00:24:57,080 --> 00:25:00,159
My father is going to punish her personally.

254
00:25:01,160 --> 00:25:04,319
-Come on!
-Alps, let's go!

255
00:25:35,480 --> 00:25:38,679
Praise be to my talented Hatun.

256
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:41,239
My Alaeddin.

257
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:43,799
My rose

258
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,959
What happened?

259
00:25:58,320 --> 00:26:01,759
Are you sick of me on day one?

260
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:05,639
Why do you look upset? Tell me.

261
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:09,599
I'm afraid about what's going to happen.

262
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:14,039
I always get you in trouble.

263
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:16,839
I always bring trouble.

264
00:26:17,120 --> 00:26:22,039
Yes. You always cause trouble for me.

265
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:31,319
But it's a sweet trouble.

266
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:35,599
Come here.

267
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:43,999
Don’t you worry.

268
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:47,559
We promised each other.

269
00:26:48,080 --> 00:26:51,799
Their evil intentions
and ambitions for the throne...

270
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:54,879
..cannot stop our love.

271
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:02,279
We will be the ones who will win.

272
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:05,639
If Allah permits, Alaeddin.

273
00:27:06,840 --> 00:27:09,239
So? What will we eat?

274
00:27:09,280 --> 00:27:12,079
I've prepared the food.

275
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:16,839
But these are the last ones from the hunt.

276
00:27:19,960 --> 00:27:22,759
The boiler will be empty tomorrow, is that so?

277
00:27:23,640 --> 00:27:27,679
Are you testing your man with hunger on day one?

278
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:31,159
Right.

279
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:35,679
If my man wanders around and picks daisies

280
00:27:35,800 --> 00:27:38,839
he will drink
water instead of eating food tomorrow.

281
00:27:38,880 --> 00:27:42,519
Okay then. I learned my lesson.

282
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:45,519
I'll go hunting tomorrow morning.

283
00:27:45,560 --> 00:27:48,199
I will bring the best foods for my Hatun.

284
00:27:48,520 --> 00:27:51,799
Well, we will see.

285
00:27:55,560 --> 00:27:58,719
Put some so we can eat, come on.

286
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:01,999
My Scholar.

287
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:04,399
You're so smart.

288
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:08,279
But we will eat together with everyone.

289
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:11,719
Is that so?

290
00:28:12,120 --> 00:28:14,279
Very well, let it be that way.

291
00:28:14,400 --> 00:28:17,199
Talented Hatun.

292
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:28,959
Alaeddin.

293
00:28:29,520 --> 00:28:32,479
Alaeddin, no.

294
00:28:32,840 --> 00:28:35,879
-Gonca.
-Bala?

295
00:28:36,560 --> 00:28:38,759
Bala.

296
00:28:39,120 --> 00:28:41,079
Bala.

297
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:44,719
-Bala.
-Osman.

298
00:28:44,840 --> 00:28:46,199
You had a nightmare.

299
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:49,719
Calm down. Just calm down.

300
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:53,039
Ibrahim and Melike.

301
00:28:53,720 --> 00:28:56,559
They were hanging

302
00:28:56,840 --> 00:28:58,879
Alaeddin and Gonca.

303
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:02,359
I ran but I couldn't get there on time.

304
00:29:02,560 --> 00:29:06,559
I couldn't get there, Osman.

305
00:29:07,360 --> 00:29:09,439
They couldn't breathe.

306
00:29:09,920 --> 00:29:13,159
They couldn't breathe, Osman.

307
00:29:14,040 --> 00:29:18,759
Come here, come.

308
00:29:22,280 --> 00:29:25,679
Who are you? Open your face.

309
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:32,519
-Boran Bey. -Brothers.

310
00:29:32,600 --> 00:29:35,519
I have something to say to Osman Bey.

311
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:37,959
How dare you come here!

312
00:29:39,320 --> 00:29:41,519
Turahan, brother!

313
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:46,399
Brother! Turahan! Stop

314
00:29:46,520 --> 00:29:50,279
-Hold him!
-I said I have something to say to Osman Bey!

315
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:54,799
Hey!

316
00:29:56,240 --> 00:29:58,759
Turahan! Stop, brother.

317
00:29:59,080 --> 00:30:00,879
Let's listen to him.

318
00:30:03,840 --> 00:30:07,079
Boran Bey, from now on

319
00:30:07,280 --> 00:30:10,559
you shouldn't have anything to say to my Bey.

320
00:30:11,760 --> 00:30:15,999
But if you want to die in the hands of my Bey...

321
00:30:16,320 --> 00:30:18,679
...let's go there, then.

322
00:30:28,920 --> 00:30:31,119
Thank you, Aykurt.

323
00:30:31,240 --> 00:30:33,759
Come on.

324
00:30:38,120 --> 00:30:41,159
This nightmare you just saw

325
00:30:41,600 --> 00:30:45,039
is a good sign.

326
00:30:45,320 --> 00:30:48,279
They both will walk a long way.

327
00:30:48,480 --> 00:30:50,439
This is a sign of it.

328
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:54,039
And you can't get Alaeddin out of your mind.

329
00:30:54,200 --> 00:30:57,599
That's why you're always dreaming about him.

330
00:30:58,120 --> 00:31:02,279
Right. Right.

331
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:07,519
What are you doing? Are you working?

332
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:11,799
I worked, my Bala. When did you see me not working?

333
00:31:11,920 --> 00:31:18,239
Every time I look
here, I see the way leading to Bursa.

334
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:23,879
While Alaeddin is a fugitive, Osman?

335
00:31:27,480 --> 00:31:30,039
You mothers always

336
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:32,999
exaggerate everything.

337
00:31:33,040 --> 00:31:34,479
Just wait.

338
00:31:34,600 --> 00:31:37,639
I didn't leave them hungry when I was raising them,

339
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:40,679
We taught them lessons.

340
00:31:40,760 --> 00:31:42,399
Don't you worry.

341
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:47,119
They had their lessons. They’ll take
care of it, don't worry.

342
00:31:48,360 --> 00:31:51,079
Right, that's right.

343
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:52,399
What about the court?

344
00:31:52,440 --> 00:31:54,559
Just wait.

345
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:58,959
First, take a look at this.

346
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:02,439
This is Mekece.

347
00:32:02,640 --> 00:32:04,959
Its location is so crucial.

348
00:32:05,040 --> 00:32:07,079
Because,

349
00:32:07,160 --> 00:32:12,079
behind this there is Bursa, and then Iznik.

350
00:32:14,760 --> 00:32:17,359
I'll move towards there.

351
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:20,839
We have many obstacles ahead of us.

352
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:24,479
Those among us, court first.

353
00:32:25,320 --> 00:32:28,199
Alliance of Germiyans and Candars.

354
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:33,239
But if they make any tricks in the court

355
00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:36,119
they will face our retaliation.

356
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:37,959
Harshly.

357
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:39,879
We will retaliate

358
00:32:40,080 --> 00:32:44,399
and then I will take Alaeddin to his mother.

359
00:32:44,560 --> 00:32:48,479
Right. They will return, if Allah permits.

360
00:32:49,520 --> 00:32:53,559
What precautions do you think about the court?

361
00:32:53,680 --> 00:32:57,359
Alaeddin thought about everything, he
prepared the Alps.

362
00:32:57,760 --> 00:33:02,399
You will see it with your own eyes,
if Allah permits.

363
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:07,719
Tell me now.
Are we going to be able to see that...

364
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:11,879
...the Turkish banner will be put in Bursa?

365
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:17,919
I don't know if we can see it, my Osman,

366
00:33:18,120 --> 00:33:22,159
you planted such a seed that

367
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:27,159
I have no doubt that the
whole world will see the Turkish banner.

368
00:33:27,400 --> 00:33:30,119
I hope so..

369
00:33:30,920 --> 00:33:33,079
-I hope so.
-So do I

370
00:33:33,120 --> 00:33:35,839
May I come in, my Bey?

371
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:39,839
Come on in, Aykurt.

372
00:33:43,200 --> 00:33:46,999
My Bey, Boran is here.

373
00:33:57,320 --> 00:34:00,879
Let's leave after night prayer.

374
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:03,479
We need to get there...

375
00:34:03,600 --> 00:34:06,319
...and determine the...

376
00:34:07,080 --> 00:34:08,759
...proofs of court.

377
00:34:08,760 --> 00:34:10,279
I have no doubt about you,

378
00:34:10,280 --> 00:34:13,839
but everyone is talking
about this court, Qadi Rukneddin Effendi.

379
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,998
It will be a difficult case for us.

380
00:34:16,040 --> 00:34:18,518
Let justice prevail.

381
00:34:18,920 --> 00:34:21,039
After that, the apocalypse may come.

382
00:34:24,239 --> 00:34:28,079
-What are you doing, dastard?
-Peace be upon you.

383
00:34:28,400 --> 00:34:30,518
Rukneddin the judge.

384
00:34:30,560 --> 00:34:32,478
Who are you?

385
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:38,998
Your death.

386
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:42,879
But not now.

387
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:47,199
Even your corpse is valuable.

388
00:35:03,440 --> 00:35:04,999
We're leaving.

389
00:35:21,520 --> 00:35:24,999
Dear judge.

390
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:18,319
My Bey.

391
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:24,679
Come.

392
00:36:32,720 --> 00:36:35,559
Come here.

393
00:36:44,960 --> 00:36:47,279
Sit down.

394
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:50,719
-My Bey.
-Sit down!

395
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:14,919
And you are also calling me your Bey, huh?

396
00:37:15,240 --> 00:37:18,799
You let my captives run away.

397
00:37:19,160 --> 00:37:22,839
You united with those against me.

398
00:37:38,640 --> 00:37:40,559
You shouldn't have done this.

399
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:05,759
Since you came here...

400
00:38:07,440 --> 00:38:09,439
...and risked death...

401
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:14,759
...you must have something to say.

402
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:18,239
I learned about the raid...

403
00:38:18,440 --> 00:38:20,759
...at the graveyard...

404
00:38:20,840 --> 00:38:24,359
...the last moment, my Bey...

405
00:38:24,480 --> 00:38:28,959
I didn't have the chance...

406
00:38:29,240 --> 00:38:32,759
I thought being among them...

407
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:35,399
...would be better than...

408
00:38:35,520 --> 00:38:38,519
...watching from a distance.

409
00:38:39,600 --> 00:38:43,279
Then you threw those arrows, huh?!

410
00:38:46,760 --> 00:38:48,559
What was your goal?

411
00:38:48,600 --> 00:38:51,999
To take the gold

412
00:38:54,320 --> 00:38:57,479
from the palace...

413
00:38:57,720 --> 00:38:59,679
Then you can

414
00:38:59,920 --> 00:39:03,759
exile me, my Bey.

415
00:39:03,840 --> 00:39:06,599
Allow me...

416
00:39:06,720 --> 00:39:10,359
Let me fulfill my last duty.

417
00:39:43,880 --> 00:39:46,279
Ibrahim Bey...

418
00:39:46,400 --> 00:39:50,319
...wants to find Shahzade Alaeddin...

419
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:52,639
...and kill him.

420
00:39:52,720 --> 00:39:54,639
I and Konur told him that...

421
00:39:55,160 --> 00:39:59,439
...we knew the secret ways, my Bey.

422
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:03,919
We were going to tell Ibrahim Bey where you...

423
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:07,519
...were when you met Shahzade Alaeddin.

424
00:40:23,480 --> 00:40:27,479
So Ibrahim Bey wants Alaeddin Bey.

425
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:32,759
We will tell him the way.

426
00:40:33,200 --> 00:40:35,319
And that way..

427
00:40:36,160 --> 00:40:39,679
...will bring Ibrahim to us.

428
00:40:42,280 --> 00:40:45,039
You will wait for us at Asbahar.

429
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:51,039
Now leave.

430
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:06,079
Yes my Bey.

431
00:41:11,280 --> 00:41:16,119
What about Olcay? Boran knows where he is.

432
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:17,559
Won't we kill him?

433
00:41:17,680 --> 00:41:19,239
No.

434
00:41:20,480 --> 00:41:22,559
Who is behind Olcay...

435
00:41:23,960 --> 00:41:27,319
We will first learn that.
We will do it after that.

436
00:41:27,720 --> 00:41:32,279
My Bey... Will you forgive Boran and Konur?

437
00:41:32,640 --> 00:41:36,719
Their punishment was to be exiled from the tribe!

438
00:41:37,280 --> 00:41:40,199
But they did not leave.

439
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:44,679
They did not leave.

440
00:41:46,240 --> 00:41:48,719
Will I forgive them...

441
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:51,959
...or not?

442
00:41:54,040 --> 00:41:56,759
Only Allah knows that.

443
00:41:57,280 --> 00:42:00,279
Germiyanoglu Border - Frontier Market

444
00:42:20,840 --> 00:42:22,599
Buldun mu Andra?
Have you found it Andra?

445
00:42:22,600 --> 00:42:24,039
Have you found it Andra?

446
00:42:24,720 --> 00:42:27,999
Buldum efendim, i§te Gonca’nin sa^lan.
Here, ma'am. Gonca's hair.

447
00:42:28,000 --> 00:42:28,839
Here, ma'am. Gonca's hair.

448
00:42:30,680 --> 00:42:34,279
Gonca...

449
00:42:38,200 --> 00:42:39,639
Revenge!

450
00:42:39,640 --> 00:42:41,079
Revenge!

451
00:42:41,160 --> 00:42:42,919
Revenge!

452
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:43,919
Revenge!

453
00:42:44,080 --> 00:42:46,799
Revenge!

454
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:24,359
Death!

455
00:43:24,360 --> 00:43:24,999
Death

456
00:43:25,280 --> 00:43:26,719
Death!

457
00:43:26,720 --> 00:43:27,039
Death!

458
00:43:27,120 --> 00:43:30,479
Gonca..

459
00:43:44,560 --> 00:43:47,039
Hatun

460
00:43:48,840 --> 00:43:53,599
Gather everything and clean it up. Right now!

461
00:43:53,960 --> 00:43:56,279
Melike Hatun

462
00:44:03,640 --> 00:44:06,559
I was reciting Kuran for our son's soul, my Bey.

463
00:44:06,720 --> 00:44:09,279
I haven't heard that you've arrived.

464
00:44:15,600 --> 00:44:18,479
May Allah accept it, Hatun.

465
00:44:19,120 --> 00:44:21,559
Your pain...

466
00:44:21,720 --> 00:44:24,199
...increases day by day, I know.

467
00:44:24,880 --> 00:44:27,079
But...

468
00:44:27,360 --> 00:44:29,479
...let your heart find peace.

469
00:44:29,560 --> 00:44:31,759
I will secure the justice.

470
00:44:32,480 --> 00:44:35,719
Unless Kayis' hearts burn...

471
00:44:36,240 --> 00:44:39,039
...my heart won't find peace.

472
00:44:39,360 --> 00:44:42,039
And our son's soul will not find peace.

473
00:44:42,120 --> 00:44:45,039
I want revenge as soon as possible.

474
00:44:45,200 --> 00:44:48,719
I will wipe their names away...

475
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:52,239
...and teach everyone a lesson.

476
00:44:58,400 --> 00:45:02,199
Walk! We are going!

477
00:45:11,920 --> 00:45:13,759
Stop!

478
00:45:14,080 --> 00:45:17,199
He will not die easily.

479
00:45:20,720 --> 00:45:22,239
Speak!

480
00:45:22,680 --> 00:45:26,199
Who are you? Who do you serve, huh?

481
00:45:26,320 --> 00:45:29,639
Where did you take
Rukneddin the judge? What is your goal?

482
00:45:29,840 --> 00:45:31,759
Look at me!

483
00:45:31,960 --> 00:45:34,999
I can drown you here in your own blood!

484
00:45:35,560 --> 00:45:41,039
Speak! Speak,
so I will take your poor life right away!

485
00:45:41,360 --> 00:45:44,119
Where did you take Rukneddin the judge?
Tell me!

486
00:45:44,200 --> 00:45:47,959
We were going to meet at Kuru Vadi
when we had it done.

487
00:45:49,840 --> 00:45:52,639
Where exactly?

488
00:45:54,560 --> 00:45:57,879
You will never be able to find it!

489
00:46:05,440 --> 00:46:07,879
Come on!

490
00:46:21,720 --> 00:46:23,799
Come on!

491
00:46:27,520 --> 00:46:29,719
How are we going to find them there?

492
00:46:29,840 --> 00:46:32,039
This is looking for a needle in a haystack.

493
00:46:32,040 --> 00:46:33,679
We have no other choice, Elcim.

494
00:46:33,800 --> 00:46:36,239
They are trying to drag Alaeddin into a pit.

495
00:46:36,280 --> 00:46:38,799
We will either take my brother out of there...

496
00:46:38,800 --> 00:46:41,239
...or we will drown there together.

497
00:46:57,000 --> 00:46:59,039
Holofira is coming this way.

498
00:46:59,240 --> 00:47:02,119
She is also involved in the abduction
of Gonca Hatun.

499
00:47:02,200 --> 00:47:04,879
She knows where she went.

500
00:47:05,320 --> 00:47:07,959
We will take this Hatun. Come on.

501
00:47:33,800 --> 00:47:34,879
Ambush.

502
00:47:35,000 --> 00:47:38,799
We are not going to let
them go! We will take the Hatun! Come on!

503
00:47:47,400 --> 00:47:50,359
I will never surrender to you!

504
00:47:59,640 --> 00:48:02,519
You

505
00:48:04,520 --> 00:48:06,799
You have nowhere to escape.

506
00:48:06,960 --> 00:48:09,919
You will tell us where
Alaeddin Bey and Gonca Hatun are.

507
00:48:10,200 --> 00:48:14,039
I don't know. I don't know. Let me go.

508
00:48:14,800 --> 00:48:16,479
Holofira Hatun..

509
00:48:16,520 --> 00:48:20,399
We know that you abducted Gonca together.

510
00:48:23,080 --> 00:48:25,959
You will tell us how you killed Shahzade Ahmed.

511
00:48:25,960 --> 00:48:28,959
You will tell us where that murderer
Alaeddin is hiding.

512
00:48:28,960 --> 00:48:30,079
Enough!

513
00:48:30,360 --> 00:48:32,679
Alaeddin is not a murderer!

514
00:48:40,040 --> 00:48:44,359
But if you don't tell me where they are, I won't
care that you are a Hatun, I will kill you.

515
00:48:48,080 --> 00:48:51,999
Alright. I'll tell you.

516
00:48:54,960 --> 00:48:57,599
They are in Kiyidibi.

517
00:49:00,400 --> 00:49:02,239
What if you are lying?

518
00:49:02,880 --> 00:49:04,559
I am not lying.

519
00:49:04,640 --> 00:49:07,119
But you are making a big mistake.

520
00:49:07,280 --> 00:49:09,479
Alaeddin is not a murderer.

521
00:49:09,520 --> 00:49:11,559
I am his witness, he is not a killer.

522
00:49:11,560 --> 00:49:13,679
When we were leaving the marketplace...

523
00:49:13,680 --> 00:49:15,159
...Ahmed was alive.

524
00:49:15,600 --> 00:49:19,159
Who killed him then? Do you also know that?

525
00:49:19,400 --> 00:49:22,799
Who was it if it was not Alaeddin Bey?

526
00:49:26,200 --> 00:49:28,479
I don't know!

527
00:49:31,520 --> 00:49:33,799
I will tell what she said to my Bey.

528
00:49:33,880 --> 00:49:37,039
You take her to the Frontier Marketplace safely.

529
00:49:39,320 --> 00:49:41,959
-Come on.
-Husrev.

530
00:49:43,480 --> 00:49:46,639
You go with Tugay.

531
00:49:47,520 --> 00:49:50,199
Osman Bey's spies are around.

532
00:49:50,880 --> 00:49:55,319
Alright. You are right.

533
00:50:16,200 --> 00:50:19,599
There are footprints here.

534
00:50:21,240 --> 00:50:23,119
My Shahzade.

535
00:50:23,480 --> 00:50:25,839
Ulcay's whip.

536
00:50:26,280 --> 00:50:28,599
It seems they clashed here.

537
00:50:29,640 --> 00:50:31,879
Is there a cave nearby, Kanyumaz?

538
00:50:32,400 --> 00:50:36,519
There are many caves
towards Dokuz Kaya la r, my Shahzade.

539
00:50:37,080 --> 00:50:41,799
Right so. They are hiding in one of the caves.

540
00:50:41,960 --> 00:50:44,279
We will check each hole, Kanyumaz.

541
00:50:44,520 --> 00:50:47,399
As you command, my Shahzade.

542
00:50:58,000 --> 00:51:00,439
Come on then.

543
00:51:00,440 --> 00:51:03,799
Let us see your skills, Alaeddin Bey.

544
00:51:04,040 --> 00:51:06,759
You will see.

545
00:51:06,800 --> 00:51:10,359
I will bring you
the most delicious catch you ever saw.

546
00:51:10,560 --> 00:51:12,519
-Is that so?
-Yes.

547
00:51:12,560 --> 00:51:14,799
Alright. I will wait for you then.

548
00:51:14,840 --> 00:51:18,839
Alright. You wait.

549
00:51:19,720 --> 00:51:21,879
My Shahzade.

550
00:51:21,960 --> 00:51:24,359
-I could've also gone.
-No.

551
00:51:24,560 --> 00:51:27,119
I will bring the catch today.

552
00:51:27,200 --> 00:51:30,079
You protect my Hatun.

553
00:51:32,360 --> 00:51:34,919
Hasan. Baysungur.

554
00:51:35,160 --> 00:51:37,439
Stay cautious.

555
00:51:51,920 --> 00:51:54,399
Come on.

556
00:52:14,240 --> 00:52:17,559
The men will arrive to the valley soon.

557
00:52:17,800 --> 00:52:21,599
We need to hurry.

558
00:52:25,320 --> 00:52:28,199
You will be sent to hell soon as well.

559
00:52:28,280 --> 00:52:29,799
Rukneddin the judge.

560
00:52:29,880 --> 00:52:32,919
Hell is a place for devils like you.

561
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:36,559
That is the place you will go in the end.

562
00:53:10,720 --> 00:53:12,719
Where will we start from?

563
00:53:12,720 --> 00:53:15,239
There are many trees. We do not have good vision.

564
00:53:15,400 --> 00:53:17,959
This valley goes to Karlidaglar.

565
00:53:18,080 --> 00:53:20,759
We know they are around here somewhere.

566
00:53:21,280 --> 00:53:23,399
Even that gives me hope.

567
00:53:23,440 --> 00:53:25,759
With Allah's permission we will find them.

568
00:53:25,880 --> 00:53:27,679
There are a lot off trees around.

569
00:53:27,720 --> 00:53:30,119
It will be hard for them to move with horses.

570
00:53:30,120 --> 00:53:33,279
However, it is good for moving without being seen.

571
00:53:33,640 --> 00:53:36,079
Whatever they want to do with the judge...

572
00:53:36,600 --> 00:53:39,479
..they are onto something secret.

573
00:53:40,520 --> 00:53:42,839
However, we will find out.

574
00:53:42,880 --> 00:53:46,519
We will find out and make them pay.

575
00:53:46,920 --> 00:53:50,439
We will reach north first.

576
00:54:12,600 --> 00:54:16,279
Thank you, Holofira.

577
00:54:16,520 --> 00:54:18,959
You did your duty.

578
00:54:19,160 --> 00:54:22,639
You were more brave
than those we called brothers once.

579
00:54:23,680 --> 00:54:25,839
After what you have done for me..

580
00:54:26,000 --> 00:54:28,159
..it was nothing, Osman Bey.

581
00:54:28,400 --> 00:54:33,519
However, you going to
Frontier Marketplace does not feel right.

582
00:54:33,800 --> 00:54:36,399
They can not touch me, you know that.

583
00:54:36,520 --> 00:54:40,039
They do not want to be bad with Emperor.

584
00:54:41,840 --> 00:54:45,839
Holofira is entrusted to us, my Bey. Do not worry.

585
00:54:51,360 --> 00:54:53,199
Osman Bey.

586
00:54:54,320 --> 00:54:56,879
Even if you do not see me as your comrade..

587
00:54:57,160 --> 00:55:00,079
..I never left your cause.

588
00:55:00,760 --> 00:55:03,759
That is why I took those gold.

589
00:55:05,640 --> 00:55:08,239
I drew the location where the gold is here.

590
00:55:08,360 --> 00:55:11,399
Let the alps go and take it.

591
00:55:17,800 --> 00:55:20,599
You think this is about gold.

592
00:55:22,000 --> 00:55:24,719
Still.

593
00:55:26,520 --> 00:55:28,839
You went against tradition.

594
00:55:28,960 --> 00:55:31,999
You went against our command.

595
00:55:33,120 --> 00:55:36,239
You fell into arrogance and spilled each
other's blood.

596
00:55:36,240 --> 00:55:38,559
There is no way for me to forgive you.

597
00:55:42,520 --> 00:55:44,559
However, I see that..

598
00:55:44,600 --> 00:55:48,239
..you do not forgive yourself neither.

599
00:55:50,480 --> 00:55:52,959
If you do not forgive us..

600
00:55:53,080 --> 00:55:57,079
..we never will, my Bey.

601
00:55:58,160 --> 00:56:00,919
If Allah permits,
we become martyrs for this cause..

602
00:56:01,440 --> 00:56:04,199
..and our Creator forgives us.

603
00:56:09,400 --> 00:56:13,759
Allow us to stay among
them until this trouble goes away, my Bey.

604
00:56:14,160 --> 00:56:18,119
Holofira. May you arrive safely.

605
00:56:27,560 --> 00:56:29,799
Bring the alps.

606
00:57:05,120 --> 00:57:07,119
My Bey.

607
00:57:07,400 --> 00:57:12,239
The news are correct Osman has sent
someone to send word to Alaeddin.

608
00:57:13,200 --> 00:57:14,239
Who?

609
00:57:14,320 --> 00:57:18,239
the Byzantine noblewoman called Holofira.

610
00:57:18,280 --> 00:57:20,839
She was there when Ahmed Bey was murdered.

611
00:57:20,920 --> 00:57:23,039
If we can make her talk before the trial..

612
00:57:23,040 --> 00:57:24,559
..it will be good for us.

613
00:57:25,240 --> 00:57:27,519
Well thought, Tugay.

614
00:57:27,600 --> 00:57:28,799
Where is the girl now?

615
00:57:28,840 --> 00:57:32,239
Now, Boran and Konur are bringing her here.

616
00:57:32,880 --> 00:57:34,839
Where is Alaeddin?

617
00:57:34,880 --> 00:57:37,439
Alaeddin is in the cave at Kayadibi, my Bey.

618
00:57:37,600 --> 00:57:42,719
First, I will kill Osman's son myself.

619
00:57:43,960 --> 00:57:46,399
Then I will kill his people..

620
00:57:47,040 --> 00:57:50,079
..for protecting him.

621
00:57:50,200 --> 00:57:53,319
-Then, you know the rest, Tugay.
-I do, my Bey.

622
00:57:53,320 --> 00:57:55,359
The rest is the field of battle.

623
00:57:55,400 --> 00:57:58,239
Take alps from me as well.

624
00:57:58,480 --> 00:58:01,319
Do not go with so few, Ibrahim Bey.

625
00:58:01,520 --> 00:58:05,199
I've got enough to break Osman's cub.

626
00:58:05,240 --> 00:58:07,439
Thank you.

627
00:58:08,280 --> 00:58:11,199
Come on!

628
00:58:23,760 --> 00:58:26,759
Traitors!

629
00:58:33,920 --> 00:58:37,279
Gonca Hatun, run!

630
00:58:37,880 --> 00:58:41,319
Hasan, take Gonca Hatun and leave!
I will stall them!

631
00:58:41,600 --> 00:58:45,719
Do not run away! You have to pay!

632
00:58:48,880 --> 00:58:52,719
Mehmed Bey, stay back.

633
00:58:56,160 --> 00:58:59,679
-Get out of the way, Baysungur.
-Stay back, Mehmed Bey.

634
00:59:05,840 --> 00:59:08,599
Gonca!

635
00:59:08,760 --> 00:59:11,719
-Gonca! Do not run! Come here!
-Run!

636
00:59:11,760 --> 00:59:13,439
Gonca!

637
00:59:13,680 --> 00:59:15,879
Mehmed Bey!

638
00:59:15,880 --> 00:59:20,799
You are making a mistake! Gonca Hatun run faster!

639
00:59:26,840 --> 00:59:28,279
Brothers.

640
00:59:44,960 --> 00:59:47,679
-Hasan!
-Run, Gonca Hatun!

641
00:59:47,720 --> 00:59:51,319
Run! Save your life!

642
00:59:56,520 --> 00:59:59,239
Gonca

643
00:59:59,560 --> 01:00:03,039
What did you do Gonca? What did you do!

644
01:00:09,240 --> 01:00:11,119
You stained our honor!

645
01:00:11,320 --> 01:00:13,319
From now on, you will be locked up!

646
01:00:13,400 --> 01:00:15,039
You can not do anything!

647
01:00:15,160 --> 01:00:17,959
I am married to Alaeddin now!

648
01:00:26,000 --> 01:00:28,359
Gonca!

649
01:00:35,800 --> 01:00:39,319
-What have you done, Gonca? -Get off!

650
01:00:40,320 --> 01:00:42,039
You heard me.

651
01:00:42,200 --> 01:00:44,199
I'm his wife now

652
01:00:44,280 --> 01:00:47,679
I've always lived with my honor.

653
01:00:48,840 --> 01:00:51,839
Besides, speaking of honor,

654
01:00:52,000 --> 01:00:54,519
...why do you think of women only?

655
01:00:56,360 --> 01:00:59,959
Were you honorable while
working with Candar and doing things...

656
01:00:59,960 --> 01:01:02,239
...behind Osman Bey's back?

657
01:01:03,480 --> 01:01:06,839
-Where is Alaaddin? Where? -Get off!

658
01:01:08,200 --> 01:01:10,119
He's gone to the tribe.

659
01:01:10,400 --> 01:01:13,079
He's going to see Osman Bey.

660
01:01:14,520 --> 01:01:18,279
If you care about me even a little,

661
01:01:18,720 --> 01:01:20,559
...leave us alone.

662
01:01:20,760 --> 01:01:23,679
-Don't mess with us.
-No.

663
01:01:23,880 --> 01:01:25,919
You won't find peace anymore, Gonca.

664
01:01:26,040 --> 01:01:28,119
If Alaaddin is a true man

665
01:01:28,320 --> 01:01:29,959
...he'll come and surrender.

666
01:01:30,160 --> 01:01:33,639
Then I'll kill him even before the trial.

667
01:01:33,960 --> 01:01:37,559
And there will be no marriage behind.

668
01:01:38,520 --> 01:01:40,119
Do you have no mercy?

669
01:01:41,440 --> 01:01:44,999
-Do you have no mercy left at all?
-Shut up!

670
01:01:45,880 --> 01:01:48,239
We're going back to the frontier market.

671
01:01:49,800 --> 01:01:51,479
-Kanyumaz.
-My Shahzade.

672
01:01:51,560 --> 01:01:53,439
Take Gonca to the horses.

673
01:01:53,720 --> 01:01:55,519
We're leaving shortly.

674
01:01:55,600 --> 01:01:57,959
As you order, my Shahzade.

675
01:01:59,840 --> 01:02:02,039
Don't touch me.

676
01:02:02,240 --> 01:02:04,199
Come on!

677
01:02:18,440 --> 01:02:20,999
Lay an ambush near the cave.

678
01:02:21,200 --> 01:02:24,519
When Alaaddin comes, kill him.

679
01:02:24,640 --> 01:02:27,279
As you order, my Shahzade.

680
01:02:32,760 --> 01:02:36,799
If Alaaddin survives, he'll come after Gonca.

681
01:02:37,240 --> 01:02:39,999
Then I'll kill him personally.

682
01:03:01,280 --> 01:03:03,399
As they say,

683
01:03:03,840 --> 01:03:08,039
...justice is putting everything where it belongs.

684
01:03:09,880 --> 01:03:15,079
So you're being
put in the grave before you die, Judge.

685
01:03:15,440 --> 01:03:19,919
You can’t overcome justice by vile actions.

686
01:03:20,200 --> 01:03:24,039
It's more important than the life.

687
01:03:24,560 --> 01:03:29,279
The fake judge taking
your place will overcome the justice.

688
01:03:29,520 --> 01:03:32,279
Even you'd be surprised to see that.

689
01:03:32,480 --> 01:03:36,479
But you're going to die.

690
01:03:36,720 --> 01:03:39,439
Allah's justice...

691
01:03:39,760 --> 01:03:43,639
His justice is everlasting.

692
01:03:43,800 --> 01:03:47,559
He will overcome you.

693
01:04:53,880 --> 01:04:57,319
Before Ahmed's body rots,

694
01:04:57,880 --> 01:05:01,119
...Alaaddin's head will fall.

695
01:05:02,200 --> 01:05:06,319
Then nothing
will be able to stop the war of beylics.

696
01:05:06,440 --> 01:05:10,439
Who attacked the inn
and looked for the judge, Ulcay Khan?

697
01:05:10,600 --> 01:05:12,679
No news from them.

698
01:05:12,960 --> 01:05:14,999
It doesn't matter.

699
01:05:15,320 --> 01:05:17,919
Judge Rukneddin is dead.

700
01:05:18,080 --> 01:05:20,279
It doesn't matter even if they all die.

701
01:05:21,080 --> 01:05:23,639
Before Judge Rukneddin's dead body is found,

702
01:05:23,800 --> 01:05:26,799
...the people after us can do nothing to us.

703
01:05:29,880 --> 01:05:34,239
Calm down. Jackal. Calm down.

704
01:05:35,760 --> 01:05:39,079
Come on

705
01:06:04,520 --> 01:06:06,879
My magic is working.

706
01:06:07,000 --> 01:06:08,879
Look there.

707
01:06:09,240 --> 01:06:12,799
They're all going to be in my hands gradually.

708
01:06:50,720 --> 01:06:53,239
Yakup Bey.

709
01:06:53,520 --> 01:06:57,039
We brought Alaaddin's
accomplice who abducted your daughter.

710
01:06:58,680 --> 01:07:02,839
Osman was taking this hatun to
Constantinople to stop her from testifying.

711
01:07:03,080 --> 01:07:05,279
Alright, Beys.

712
01:07:05,480 --> 01:07:09,399
You proved to be on the side of justice.

713
01:07:10,320 --> 01:07:13,039
You will be rewarded.

714
01:07:15,080 --> 01:07:18,279
Killers.

715
01:07:18,680 --> 01:07:22,519
You all will get your shares from my wrath.

716
01:07:22,640 --> 01:07:24,999
All of you.

717
01:07:28,960 --> 01:07:30,839
Andra.

718
01:07:31,080 --> 01:07:35,159
-You snake!
-You are the snake!

719
01:07:35,480 --> 01:07:39,399
You helped Alaaddin while he was killing
my son, huh?

720
01:07:39,680 --> 01:07:40,768
Ha?

721
01:07:40,780 --> 01:07:44,079
Your son was
alive while leaving the frontier market.

722
01:07:45,080 --> 01:07:46,839
Someone else killed him.

723
01:07:47,040 --> 01:07:50,719
You're lying! Lying!

724
01:07:51,680 --> 01:07:54,039
Melike Hatun!

725
01:07:59,600 --> 01:08:03,159
This is not a time when we should act with anger.

726
01:08:03,640 --> 01:08:06,599
Stop now.

727
01:08:08,040 --> 01:08:11,119
She's a Byzantine princess.

728
01:08:12,520 --> 01:08:14,879
When the time comes

729
01:08:15,240 --> 01:08:18,238
...she will serve us.

730
01:08:24,720 --> 01:08:26,479
Fine.

731
01:08:27,000 --> 01:08:29,759
So be it.

732
01:08:30,200 --> 01:08:32,759
If she's to testify,

733
01:08:33,000 --> 01:08:35,959
...I'm putting my sword down.

734
01:08:38,359 --> 01:08:41,479
-But..
-But..

735
01:08:42,680 --> 01:08:45,719
If she tells lies

736
01:08:46,040 --> 01:08:49,439
...we will put the rope around her neck.

737
01:08:50,160 --> 01:08:53,399
Don't be worrying, Melike Hatun.

738
01:09:16,279 --> 01:09:19,479
Thank You, my Allah!

739
01:09:19,880 --> 01:09:22,599
Our stomachs are going to be filled today.

740
01:09:28,000 --> 01:09:29,959
Guice?

741
01:09:30,160 --> 01:09:32,799
-What’s the matter?
-Alaaddin Bey.

742
01:09:32,920 --> 01:09:34,879
-Mehmed Bey came here.
-And?

743
01:09:35,040 --> 01:09:36,759
He took Gonca Hatun away.

744
01:09:36,840 --> 01:09:37,879
What are you saying?

745
01:09:38,040 --> 01:09:41,399
Alps laid an ambush near the cave to kill you.

746
01:09:41,880 --> 01:09:43,639
Where have they taken my Gonca?

747
01:09:43,760 --> 01:09:45,799
To the frontier market.

748
01:09:45,840 --> 01:09:48,999
What now, Alaaddin Bey?

749
01:09:49,560 --> 01:09:52,038
I know what to do.

750
01:09:53,040 --> 01:09:55,279
I won't leave my hatun to them.

751
01:09:55,560 --> 01:09:57,719
I won't!

752
01:09:58,480 --> 01:10:00,879
Don't do this, Alaaddin Bey!

753
01:10:01,720 --> 01:10:03,399
They won’t let you live.

754
01:10:03,400 --> 01:10:05,559
Only Allah can know that!

755
01:10:05,600 --> 01:10:07,639
Come on!

756
01:10:13,280 --> 01:10:15,799
Alaaddin!

757
01:10:20,360 --> 01:10:22,439
Alaaddin!

758
01:10:26,720 --> 01:10:29,239
Alaaddin, come out!

759
01:10:31,120 --> 01:10:34,159
Come out, my son's killer!

760
01:10:39,560 --> 01:10:41,839
There are no killers here.

761
01:10:46,440 --> 01:10:49,319
No killers in my family either.

762
01:10:50,720 --> 01:10:53,679
But don't push us too much.

763
01:10:54,840 --> 01:10:57,479
Don't harm the alps!

764
01:10:58,440 --> 01:11:00,719
But the blood of Ulcay's dogs...

765
01:11:00,800 --> 01:11:02,519
...is halal to you!

766
01:11:02,600 --> 01:11:05,879
This is the fight of
justice! Attack, warriors! Show no mercy!

767
01:11:05,920 --> 01:11:08,559
Come here, Ulcay's dogs!

768
01:11:08,600 --> 01:11:12,919
Allah is Eternal!

769
01:11:20,480 --> 01:11:24,359
I'm not lying. Alaaddin Bey didn't kill anyone.

770
01:11:27,400 --> 01:11:30,159
Gonca and he loved each other.

771
01:11:30,600 --> 01:11:33,919
So they ran away. That's all.

772
01:11:34,720 --> 01:11:36,839
Holofira Hatun.

773
01:11:37,120 --> 01:11:39,439
Don’t go too far.

774
01:11:39,800 --> 01:11:41,559
Do not.

775
01:11:41,800 --> 01:11:45,799
Don't you
attempt to defend those killers against me.

776
01:11:51,880 --> 01:11:53,399
Take her..

777
01:11:53,640 --> 01:11:56,479
...to the cage tent!

778
01:11:57,080 --> 01:11:59,559
I know how to make you speak.

779
01:12:01,360 --> 01:12:03,599
Come on!

780
01:12:15,320 --> 01:12:18,399
You surprised me, Beys.

781
01:12:21,360 --> 01:12:24,679
You turned out to have noble blood.

782
01:12:25,800 --> 01:12:28,719
You're on the side of the right.

783
01:12:31,000 --> 01:12:35,759
From now on, I want to see you two on my side.

784
01:12:35,960 --> 01:12:38,679
You should know that.

785
01:12:39,720 --> 01:12:44,199
While Osman's children are as arrogant as him,

786
01:12:45,080 --> 01:12:48,919
...doing the otherwise wouldn't suit us, Yakup Bey.

787
01:12:49,520 --> 01:12:51,799
We always avoid the arrogance, Yakup Bey.

788
01:12:52,000 --> 01:12:54,279
It's an honor for us to be on your side.

789
01:12:54,400 --> 01:12:57,479
Alright then. Be my guests.

790
01:13:28,800 --> 01:13:31,919
But you will never get smarter.

791
01:13:35,120 --> 01:13:39,199
You first let the Shahzade beat you, then me.

792
01:13:40,200 --> 01:13:42,559
But... getting hurt is your fate.

793
01:13:42,600 --> 01:13:44,879
Sure... If you are going to stand against us.

794
01:13:45,040 --> 01:13:49,479
You were not able to crush me, but I
will crush you all under my feet Cerkutay.

795
01:14:02,000 --> 01:14:06,199
Enough! Enough, Ibrahim Bey!

796
01:14:07,560 --> 01:14:09,959
Drop your sword.

797
01:14:36,800 --> 01:14:40,159
Do you want my life...

798
01:14:40,440 --> 01:14:44,239
...after taking my son's life?

799
01:14:46,320 --> 01:14:48,679
Take it then.

800
01:14:49,560 --> 01:14:52,039
But..

801
01:14:52,240 --> 01:14:55,559
Your debt to Candar is increasing, know that.

802
01:14:55,680 --> 01:14:58,239
My intention was never...

803
01:14:58,640 --> 01:15:02,439
...to take your life.

804
01:15:02,520 --> 01:15:05,439
If'it were, I would have done it a thousand times.

805
01:15:06,480 --> 01:15:08,959
I told you to wait until the trial.

806
01:15:09,080 --> 01:15:10,959
Is that so?

807
01:15:11,200 --> 01:15:13,359
You captured us, Osman Bey!

808
01:15:13,360 --> 01:15:16,719
What would have changed if I hadn't?

809
01:15:17,040 --> 01:15:19,319
You're gathering your people and army...

810
01:15:19,480 --> 01:15:22,079
...and getting ready for war. Don't I know that?

811
01:15:22,120 --> 01:15:26,639
I am a father! I lost my son!

812
01:15:26,680 --> 01:15:28,639
Ibrahim Bey!

813
01:15:29,400 --> 01:15:30,919
Enough now.

814
01:15:30,960 --> 01:15:34,919
Stop hiding behind your son's pain.

815
01:15:35,120 --> 01:15:37,319
It doesn't suit you.

816
01:15:37,440 --> 01:15:39,319
I will be a curse to you...

817
01:15:40,600 --> 01:15:43,559
...and your so-called state...

818
01:15:43,840 --> 01:15:46,919
...which is just a tribe looking like village!

819
01:15:47,080 --> 01:15:49,679
Ibrahim Bey.

820
01:15:50,840 --> 01:15:53,159
You destroyed the Cobanogullari...

821
01:15:53,280 --> 01:15:56,079
...with the help of Ilkhanate...

822
01:15:56,120 --> 01:15:59,839
...and now you sit on the Beylic chair.

823
01:16:03,240 --> 01:16:05,959
We don't wear leashes around our necks.

824
01:16:06,600 --> 01:16:08,519
We will not bow to you...

825
01:16:08,760 --> 01:16:10,639
...or Olcaytu.

826
01:16:10,760 --> 01:16:12,919
Know your place, Osman Bey!

827
01:16:13,000 --> 01:16:16,359
What kind of accusation is that?
-You should know your place!

828
01:16:16,640 --> 01:16:19,639
I know why you came here.

829
01:16:19,680 --> 01:16:23,239
You came to bring trouble to my lands.

830
01:16:23,400 --> 01:16:26,439
You even planned
that wedding for your evil alliance.

831
01:16:27,320 --> 01:16:29,279
Right!

832
01:16:29,520 --> 01:16:31,639
Admit it!

833
01:16:32,200 --> 01:16:37,039
You ruined our wedding you killed my son!

834
01:16:37,240 --> 01:16:40,039
No, no, Ibrahim Bey!

835
01:16:40,280 --> 01:16:44,959
I arranged Alaeddin and
Gonca's marriage to prevent the wedding.

836
01:16:46,320 --> 01:16:49,759
They are married now. But know this.

837
01:16:50,440 --> 01:16:53,639
We didn't kill your son.

838
01:16:55,040 --> 01:16:57,039
Now make your decision.

839
01:16:57,160 --> 01:16:59,039
Will you come with us to court...

840
01:16:59,800 --> 01:17:03,479
...or will you die here?

841
01:17:03,920 --> 01:17:08,719
You can't stop the bloodshed, Osman Bey.

842
01:17:09,040 --> 01:17:11,239
Your game was...

843
01:17:12,640 --> 01:17:15,119
...ruined by the blood of my Ahmed.

844
01:17:15,360 --> 01:17:18,279
Don't you do that! Enough!

845
01:17:18,520 --> 01:17:20,959
The innocence of Alaeddin will be revealed.

846
01:17:21,040 --> 01:17:23,519
And you will leave my lands.

847
01:17:23,640 --> 01:17:27,959
Drop your sword!

848
01:17:28,240 --> 01:17:30,639
Drop it!

849
01:17:40,080 --> 01:17:42,199
Yes.

850
01:17:46,000 --> 01:17:48,359
Alps!

851
01:17:48,720 --> 01:17:52,039
Take Ibrahim Bey and his Alps...

852
01:17:53,440 --> 01:17:56,719
...the way they deserve.

853
01:17:58,920 --> 01:18:01,519
Birds will feed on...

854
01:18:01,800 --> 01:18:04,359
...the others' bodies.

855
01:18:04,480 --> 01:18:08,679
-Yes my Bey.
-Yes my Bey.

856
01:18:39,400 --> 01:18:42,399
Germiyanoglu Border - Frontier Market

857
01:18:44,360 --> 01:18:47,999
My son's blood was shed on these dowries.

858
01:18:56,560 --> 01:18:58,359
Gonca..

859
01:18:58,360 --> 01:18:58,799
Gonca...

860
01:18:58,880 --> 01:19:00,799
I will burn you and...

861
01:19:00,920 --> 01:19:04,479
...your lover just like these dowries!

862
01:19:04,920 --> 01:19:08,399
You will beg to me to die!

863
01:19:43,120 --> 01:19:45,919
Walk!

864
01:19:57,160 --> 01:19:59,839
Come on!

865
01:20:08,080 --> 01:20:10,639
The day is today.

866
01:20:12,040 --> 01:20:16,599
My son... The one who caused this has arrived.

867
01:20:17,280 --> 01:20:21,239
The one who shed your blood will also come.

868
01:20:21,400 --> 01:20:24,399
He will come.

869
01:20:42,080 --> 01:20:46,559
Apparently my son made his move before Ibrahim Bey.

870
01:20:49,000 --> 01:20:52,719
He will come soon.

871
01:21:04,240 --> 01:21:06,399
You've come back...

872
01:21:06,560 --> 01:21:09,959
...to your home again.

873
01:21:10,280 --> 01:21:12,879
Did you think you could escape from me?

874
01:21:13,080 --> 01:21:17,439
This isn't my home.

875
01:21:18,120 --> 01:21:21,719
She is not even embarrassed!

876
01:21:21,760 --> 01:21:24,279
You snake...

877
01:21:25,480 --> 01:21:27,799
You caused the death of my son!

878
01:21:28,080 --> 01:21:32,159
Know your place, Melike Hatun!

879
01:21:32,240 --> 01:21:35,399
Who are you to touch me, huh?

880
01:21:36,680 --> 01:21:41,119
I'll cut that snake tongue of yours, Gonca.

881
01:21:41,760 --> 01:21:45,039
You did not obey me.

882
01:21:45,120 --> 01:21:48,639
You embarrassed me.

883
01:21:52,160 --> 01:21:55,479
You united with
that murderer Alaeddin and ran away.

884
01:21:55,600 --> 01:21:58,999
How can you still say those things?

885
01:21:59,720 --> 01:22:03,119
Alaeddin is not a killer!

886
01:22:03,200 --> 01:22:05,039
He didn't kill Ahmed!

887
01:22:05,160 --> 01:22:07,599
You're still lying.

888
01:22:07,680 --> 01:22:11,559
But I know how to make you talk.

889
01:22:12,200 --> 01:22:14,799
Your honour... -Don't you dare!

890
01:22:15,120 --> 01:22:17,199
Don’t!

891
01:22:17,720 --> 01:22:21,479
You don’t have the right to insult my honor, Hatun!

892
01:22:22,080 --> 01:22:24,639
You're the one who asked for the hand of a girl...

893
01:22:24,680 --> 01:22:29,599
...who loved someone
else without asking or seeking permission!

894
01:22:30,640 --> 01:22:34,279
We'll see.

895
01:22:41,360 --> 01:22:45,359
I haven't committed
any dishonorable act, thanks to Allah.

896
01:22:45,640 --> 01:22:48,519
I left and..

897
01:22:48,600 --> 01:22:50,799
...married the man I loved!

898
01:22:54,920 --> 01:22:57,679
What did you do?

899
01:22:58,360 --> 01:23:01,439
How could you disobey me?

900
01:23:08,600 --> 01:23:10,479
You..

901
01:23:10,600 --> 01:23:15,239
You ruined me, Gonca.

902
01:23:17,200 --> 01:23:18,719
Now...

903
01:23:20,240 --> 01:23:22,959
...I don't have a daughter like you.

904
01:23:27,840 --> 01:23:30,879
Traitor.

905
01:23:31,800 --> 01:23:35,439
I did not betray anyone.

906
01:23:35,840 --> 01:23:41,839
Hit me! Go on! Hit me! -Gonca! -Don't! Hit me!

907
01:23:43,280 --> 01:23:45,879
You cannot hurt me!

908
01:23:45,920 --> 01:23:48,199
You said..

909
01:23:48,280 --> 01:23:51,679
...you did not have a daughter like me...

910
01:23:54,040 --> 01:23:56,559
Now I don’t have a father like you!

911
01:23:56,800 --> 01:23:59,119
Don't, father!

912
01:24:15,320 --> 01:24:18,639
Take her to the caged tent.

913
01:24:21,440 --> 01:24:24,559
The judge will decide what will happen to her.

914
01:24:42,840 --> 01:24:46,399
My child's blood is in Alaeddin's hands, Osman.

915
01:24:46,600 --> 01:24:50,159
Even if you don't believe it, he's a murderer.

916
01:24:50,240 --> 01:24:54,239
But by protecting him, you ruin your afterlife.

917
01:24:54,360 --> 01:24:58,919
Ibrahim Bey, this is the bridge of As-Sirat.

918
01:24:59,040 --> 01:25:03,479
Do not try to kill my
child, the consequences will be heavy.

919
01:25:03,880 --> 01:25:05,999
Look.

920
01:25:07,720 --> 01:25:09,679
Alaeddin is innocent.

921
01:25:09,800 --> 01:25:12,159
You'll see it one day.

922
01:25:12,240 --> 01:25:15,639
After all, the murderer is clear for me.

923
01:25:15,800 --> 01:25:19,119
When the court is set up and the verdict is given

924
01:25:19,200 --> 01:25:22,239
I'll punish him with my own hands.

925
01:25:27,640 --> 01:25:30,239
-Osman Bey.
-I hope nothing's bad.

926
01:25:30,280 --> 01:25:34,479
Guice Hatun. She's Gonca Hatun's friend, my Bey.

927
01:25:34,760 --> 01:25:38,759
Osman Bey. Mehmed Bey kidnapped Gonca Hatun.

928
01:25:40,200 --> 01:25:42,239
So, Alaeddin?

929
01:25:42,440 --> 01:25:43,559
How's Alaeddin?

930
01:25:43,560 --> 01:25:46,919
They kidnapped Gonca
Hatun while Alaeddin Bey was not there.

931
01:25:46,920 --> 01:25:50,359
They went after him too, but he got rid of them.

932
01:25:50,680 --> 01:25:53,759
He went after them, to the Frontier Marketplace.

933
01:25:55,360 --> 01:25:57,879
Thankfully.

934
01:25:58,080 --> 01:26:01,199
Now the justice will be done.

935
01:26:01,320 --> 01:26:03,599
Soon he will be captured.

936
01:26:03,720 --> 01:26:06,679
That's enough! That's enough!

937
01:26:06,760 --> 01:26:08,679
I kept quiet until now.

938
01:26:08,760 --> 01:26:11,999
But if my child gets hurt...

939
01:26:12,200 --> 01:26:16,879
...then my wrath will be heavy, Ibrahim Bey.

940
01:26:17,280 --> 01:26:20,439
Keep that in mind.

941
01:26:20,480 --> 01:26:22,319
Take Ibrahim Bey to the tribe.

942
01:26:22,360 --> 01:26:24,559
Yes, my Bey. Come on.

943
01:26:24,680 --> 01:26:27,359
What are we going to do now, my Bey?

944
01:26:27,440 --> 01:26:31,999
Alaeddin might do anything to take Gonca.

945
01:26:32,560 --> 01:26:37,879
We will not jackals get him. Come on, move.

946
01:27:05,880 --> 01:27:08,999
Please don't do any
madness and come after me, Alaeddin.

947
01:27:09,120 --> 01:27:10,879
Please don't.

948
01:27:10,920 --> 01:27:13,999
He’s not brave enough to surrender.

949
01:27:14,960 --> 01:27:18,159
But I thought you were brave.

950
01:27:19,560 --> 01:27:21,959
How could you do this to usz Gonca?

951
01:27:22,000 --> 01:27:24,999
If you were as brave enough as Alaeddin,

952
01:27:25,360 --> 01:27:28,759
you'd have stood behind me and be my brother.

953
01:27:29,120 --> 01:27:31,279
You betrayed us!

954
01:27:31,360 --> 01:27:35,359
-How can you still talk?
-I didn't betray you.

955
01:27:35,600 --> 01:27:38,439
I loved him.

956
01:27:39,920 --> 01:27:42,999
I just loved him.

957
01:27:44,080 --> 01:27:46,999
But what do you know about love?

958
01:27:48,160 --> 01:27:51,119
I saw it.

959
01:27:51,800 --> 01:27:53,799
I saw it

960
01:27:54,280 --> 01:27:56,999
when I looked at Alaeddin

961
01:27:58,520 --> 01:28:01,439
Orhan Bey and Fatma.

962
01:28:02,640 --> 01:28:06,599
You've never loved me, Mehmed Bey.

963
01:28:10,080 --> 01:28:13,319
You've never loved your household, Gonca.

964
01:28:16,160 --> 01:28:20,479
-You embarrassed us.
-I loved you.

965
01:28:21,200 --> 01:28:24,319
I loved you more than anything else.

966
01:28:24,440 --> 01:28:26,519
But what did y'all do?

967
01:28:27,040 --> 01:28:29,319
What did you do?

968
01:28:29,360 --> 01:28:31,639
First you crushed me.

969
01:28:31,760 --> 01:28:35,639
Was it enough? It was not!

970
01:28:36,480 --> 01:28:38,759
Then you broke me.

971
01:28:38,880 --> 01:28:41,239
But that was not enough for you!

972
01:28:41,280 --> 01:28:43,639
You tore me apart!

973
01:28:43,680 --> 01:28:45,639
I loved you, sister.

974
01:28:46,040 --> 01:28:48,759
I protected you from even the wind.

975
01:28:50,080 --> 01:28:52,679
Just so you don't risk yourself for someone else.

976
01:28:52,800 --> 01:28:55,879
I kept you away
from Alaeddin just because I love you.

977
01:28:56,360 --> 01:28:59,319
But it's all in vain.

978
01:28:59,480 --> 01:29:02,399
Love blinded you.

979
01:29:04,640 --> 01:29:07,439
You can’t see the truth.

980
01:29:37,200 --> 01:29:38,999
Gunduz Bey.

981
01:29:39,040 --> 01:29:41,679
Where is Osman Bey? What's going on?

982
01:29:42,000 --> 01:29:45,399
Gonca Hatun and alps were caught.

983
01:29:45,560 --> 01:29:48,319
What are you saying, Gunduz Bey?

984
01:29:49,160 --> 01:29:53,559
-What about Alaeddin? -He went after them.

985
01:29:53,720 --> 01:29:56,119
Osman Bey went after him.

986
01:29:56,160 --> 01:29:59,319
He's afraid that he will surrender.

987
01:30:00,120 --> 01:30:04,319
-Mother, my brother won't stay there.
-My Allah, protect them.

988
01:30:04,320 --> 01:30:08,079
He will not let Gonca alone with them.

989
01:30:08,280 --> 01:30:11,479
He will surrender.

990
01:30:12,560 --> 01:30:15,239
Bala Hatun!

991
01:30:15,640 --> 01:30:18,559
You will not be able to spoil justice!

992
01:30:19,240 --> 01:30:21,879
My son's death will be avenged.

993
01:30:22,000 --> 01:30:26,439
Sooner or later your child will die.

994
01:30:26,840 --> 01:30:28,879
While we have you

995
01:30:28,960 --> 01:30:33,599
they cannot hurt my child or my daughter-in-law.

996
01:30:33,800 --> 01:30:35,879
You will be treated

997
01:30:36,040 --> 01:30:38,679
as they are treated, Ibrahim Bey.

998
01:30:38,760 --> 01:30:40,879
Very well.

999
01:30:41,000 --> 01:30:45,399
So you are ignoring the

1000
01:30:45,560 --> 01:30:47,999
vile and dastard action

1001
01:30:48,080 --> 01:30:50,239
your child did.

1002
01:30:50,560 --> 01:30:53,799
You're protecting him!

1003
01:30:56,720 --> 01:30:59,679
Both your heart

1004
01:30:59,960 --> 01:31:02,959
and justice are rotten.

1005
01:31:03,880 --> 01:31:08,439
Enough! Know your place, Ibrahim Bey!

1006
01:31:08,720 --> 01:31:11,239
My child is innocent.

1007
01:31:11,560 --> 01:31:15,759
And we will always protect our children.

1008
01:31:16,400 --> 01:31:20,519
Don't make any mistake and say a word.

1009
01:31:22,760 --> 01:31:26,359
-Take him.
-Come on.

1010
01:31:34,400 --> 01:31:38,599
Bala Hatun! You will pay for this!

1011
01:31:38,760 --> 01:31:42,919
We will see who will pay, Ibrahim Bey!

1012
01:31:45,200 --> 01:31:47,439
We will see.

1013
01:31:49,040 --> 01:31:53,199
Mother. Should we go
to the Frontier Marketplace for my brother?

1014
01:31:53,200 --> 01:31:57,079
Wait, daughter. Let's wait for your father first.

1015
01:32:15,240 --> 01:32:17,879
I’m here, my Gonca.

1016
01:32:17,920 --> 01:32:20,599
I'll not leave you alone.

1017
01:33:16,000 --> 01:33:19,239
Murderer!

1018
01:33:31,160 --> 01:33:35,119
How dare you kidnap my sister?

1019
01:33:38,360 --> 01:33:41,759
You ruined him, you ruined my sister!

1020
01:33:42,000 --> 01:33:45,679
Alaeddin, what have you done?

1021
01:33:47,680 --> 01:33:50,479
Come on!

1022
01:33:51,720 --> 01:33:54,159
Open the way.

1023
01:33:54,240 --> 01:33:56,799
Open the way!

1024
01:34:05,520 --> 01:34:09,319
My Allah, please protect Alaeddin.

1025
01:34:09,680 --> 01:34:12,639
-Who will save you from me now?
-Don't you dare!

1026
01:34:12,760 --> 01:34:14,839
Don't you dare!

1027
01:34:15,160 --> 01:34:18,479
Don’t you dare make any move!

1028
01:34:38,080 --> 01:34:40,639
Are you going to take the life of another child?

1029
01:34:40,680 --> 01:34:42,399
Yakup Bey.

1030
01:34:42,560 --> 01:34:46,319
-If Alaeddin gets hurt.
-He will!

1031
01:34:46,600 --> 01:34:48,799
He will get hurt.

1032
01:34:48,880 --> 01:34:52,679
He will die as my son did.

1033
01:35:01,520 --> 01:35:02,759
Then...

1034
01:35:14,080 --> 01:35:16,959
..your Bey, Ibrahim Bey..

1035
01:35:23,720 --> 01:35:26,679
..he will die too.

1036
01:35:28,920 --> 01:35:32,479
Think about it well.

1037
01:35:33,040 --> 01:35:34,479
Your son...

1038
01:35:35,320 --> 01:35:38,839
...comes and gives in to our justice.

1039
01:35:41,680 --> 01:35:45,959
You are holding Ibrahim Bey for nothing.

1040
01:35:52,760 --> 01:35:55,719
The wisest of ulemas..

1041
01:35:55,800 --> 01:35:58,919
..Rukneddin the judge is coming.

1042
01:36:10,400 --> 01:36:15,279
First, everyone drop your weapons.

1043
01:36:17,240 --> 01:36:20,959
If justice was found with sword..

1044
01:36:21,040 --> 01:36:23,759
..we would've wear it ourselves.

1045
01:36:23,800 --> 01:36:28,199
And if you wanted to solve your issue with swords..

1046
01:36:28,280 --> 01:36:31,199
..then why did you call me for?

1047
01:36:34,920 --> 01:36:38,679
Welcome, dear judge.

1048
01:36:38,880 --> 01:36:41,799
Drop them!

1049
01:36:45,880 --> 01:36:48,999
Do you want a trial..

1050
01:36:50,480 --> 01:36:54,279
..or should we deal here.

1051
01:36:59,680 --> 01:37:03,559
If I were to deal with you..

1052
01:37:04,240 --> 01:37:06,999
..I would've had your head at the tribe.

1053
01:37:17,480 --> 01:37:19,999
Tell us, dear judge.

1054
01:37:20,120 --> 01:37:24,639
No one will touch anyone until the trial.

1055
01:37:25,520 --> 01:37:29,599
Will you do the trial here?

1056
01:37:29,760 --> 01:37:32,759
This here is not fit for the trial.

1057
01:37:32,800 --> 01:37:35,959
A lot of blood can be spilled here.

1058
01:37:36,080 --> 01:37:38,959
I will decide the location.

1059
01:37:39,080 --> 01:37:42,119
I will let you know tomorrow.

1060
01:37:42,200 --> 01:37:44,359
You will enter the trial without swords.

1061
01:37:44,520 --> 01:37:46,519
Justice will be done.

1062
01:37:46,680 --> 01:37:53,239
Dear judge is right!

1063
01:37:53,560 --> 01:37:56,039
Alright, dear judge.

1064
01:38:03,720 --> 01:38:06,159
I will get him back just as I delivered him.

1065
01:38:06,560 --> 01:38:09,039
Otherwise, if something happens..

1066
01:38:11,520 --> 01:38:15,919
..you can not pay for it.

1067
01:38:19,760 --> 01:38:21,999
Tomorrow, everything will be decided..

1068
01:38:22,560 --> 01:38:26,119
..at the trial.

1069
01:38:26,440 --> 01:38:28,799
Osman Bey.

1070
01:38:43,560 --> 01:38:46,519
-Son.
-My Bey.

1071
01:38:56,880 --> 01:38:59,599
I trust you, father.

1072
01:39:03,280 --> 01:39:05,399
Your innocence will be revealed.

1073
01:39:07,040 --> 01:39:08,759
I will come back to get you.

1074
01:39:08,960 --> 01:39:12,159
If Allah permits, my Bey.

1075
01:39:21,680 --> 01:39:23,879
Father.

1076
01:39:25,520 --> 01:39:28,719
Take good care of this.

1077
01:39:37,920 --> 01:39:40,359
Do not worry.

1078
01:39:41,120 --> 01:39:43,839
I will keep it safe.

1079
01:39:51,120 --> 01:39:54,759
-Cerkutay!
-My Bey!

1080
01:39:55,160 --> 01:39:57,519
Come on.

1081
01:40:08,840 --> 01:40:11,679
Take him!

1082
01:40:47,160 --> 01:40:50,599
Sun will go down soon.
There is no trace of the judge.

1083
01:40:50,680 --> 01:40:52,999
They must've been at north.

1084
01:40:53,080 --> 01:40:55,239
Where are they?

1085
01:40:55,360 --> 01:40:57,079
Where did they take the judge?

1086
01:40:57,320 --> 01:41:00,079
Who are these men, Orhan? What will we do now?

1087
01:41:00,160 --> 01:41:01,679
I do not know, Elcim Hatun.

1088
01:41:01,960 --> 01:41:03,759
Only thing I know..

1089
01:41:03,880 --> 01:41:07,479
..is that my brother's life, Alaeddin's
life is in danger.

1090
01:41:07,680 --> 01:41:11,799
We will not know about their
intentions, unless we find Rukneddin the judge.

1091
01:41:13,680 --> 01:41:16,519
We will check each tree if needed!

1092
01:41:16,720 --> 01:41:19,319
We will find them, come on.

1093
01:41:41,320 --> 01:41:44,159
Elcim Hatun!

1094
01:41:51,040 --> 01:41:53,519
This is the same bead ball as the one at the inn.

1095
01:41:53,720 --> 01:41:56,119
Rukneddin the judge.

1096
01:41:56,720 --> 01:41:58,759
Has left trace for us.

1097
01:41:58,840 --> 01:42:00,879
It seems he wants us to find him.

1098
01:42:00,960 --> 01:42:04,959
Come on. We will look for tracks.

1099
01:42:08,400 --> 01:42:11,799
There, found you.

1100
01:42:17,080 --> 01:42:21,399
This way! Come on, to horses!

1101
01:42:35,520 --> 01:42:38,399
Where are they.

1102
01:42:39,800 --> 01:42:42,959
They must've gone anywhere.

1103
01:42:45,880 --> 01:42:48,839
What is that?

1104
01:43:07,040 --> 01:43:09,039
The soil is freshly dug

1105
01:43:09,120 --> 01:43:11,439
They stepped on it with horses.

1106
01:43:24,440 --> 01:43:28,399
Come on, in the name of Allah.

1107
01:43:38,600 --> 01:43:40,759
Allah.

1108
01:43:41,000 --> 01:43:44,119
My Allah, protect us.

1109
01:44:03,800 --> 01:44:07,039
Rukneddin the judge.

1110
01:44:43,240 --> 01:44:45,039
This is our..

1111
01:44:45,120 --> 01:44:48,399
..paper we sent for the trial.

1112
01:44:48,600 --> 01:44:50,679
Look here.

1113
01:44:50,800 --> 01:44:53,399
It has his signature here.

1114
01:44:53,600 --> 01:44:57,079
He even tried to do bring justice while dying.

1115
01:44:59,120 --> 01:45:02,079
Scoundrels.

1116
01:45:05,680 --> 01:45:07,799
They killed him like cowards!

1117
01:45:07,880 --> 01:45:10,359
They played tricks like cowards!

1118
01:45:10,680 --> 01:45:12,439
Someone..

1119
01:45:12,640 --> 01:45:16,839
..someone does not want this trial to happen.

1120
01:45:16,960 --> 01:45:20,719
Someone does not want this trial.

1121
01:45:21,240 --> 01:45:23,159
Or, the other way.

1122
01:45:23,880 --> 01:45:26,479
Someone..

1123
01:45:26,720 --> 01:45:30,239
..wants to see this trial with their own judge.

1124
01:45:31,640 --> 01:45:33,879
Alaeddin.

1125
01:45:38,680 --> 01:45:41,519
Alaeddin.

1126
01:45:43,200 --> 01:45:46,599
-To the horses, come on!
-Orhan!

1127
01:45:46,880 --> 01:45:49,799
-We have a day's road, how will we catch up?
-We will.

1128
01:45:50,000 --> 01:45:52,679
We will catch up no matter what, Elcim Hatun.

1129
01:45:52,920 --> 01:45:54,599
My brother's life..

1130
01:45:54,720 --> 01:45:59,599
..my Alaeddin's life is in my hands.

1131
01:46:20,520 --> 01:46:22,999
Osman.

1132
01:46:23,080 --> 01:46:24,759
Where is Alaeddin?

1133
01:46:24,920 --> 01:46:27,719
Alaeddin surrendered.

1134
01:46:28,320 --> 01:46:30,159
There will be a trial tomorrow.

1135
01:46:30,280 --> 01:46:32,279
He is at Frontier Marketplace for now.

1136
01:46:32,400 --> 01:46:34,599
The trial..

1137
01:46:34,680 --> 01:46:36,959
..will be at the place..

1138
01:46:37,000 --> 01:46:39,959
..where the judge will decide, they said.

1139
01:46:40,400 --> 01:46:42,599
Do not worry.

1140
01:46:42,720 --> 01:46:45,799
Father.

1141
01:46:45,840 --> 01:46:49,879
They will not let my brother in peace there.

1142
01:46:49,920 --> 01:46:52,559
They can not do anything.

1143
01:46:52,600 --> 01:46:55,039
We have Ibrahim Bey.

1144
01:46:55,080 --> 01:46:58,039
Your brother's innocence will be proven.

1145
01:46:58,160 --> 01:47:00,399
Do not worry, my dear daughter.

1146
01:47:00,480 --> 01:47:02,439
They have been blinded.

1147
01:47:02,520 --> 01:47:04,759
They will not want to see the truth.

1148
01:47:04,920 --> 01:47:07,759
I fear that they will try to do traitorous acts.

1149
01:47:07,840 --> 01:47:10,679
What if the judge does not provide justice?

1150
01:47:10,760 --> 01:47:12,399
What if he decides..

1151
01:47:12,440 --> 01:47:14,359
..may Allah prevent it, father.

1152
01:47:14,720 --> 01:47:16,399
Do not worry.

1153
01:47:16,480 --> 01:47:19,239
We do not doubt the judge's justice.

1154
01:47:19,320 --> 01:47:21,399
However..

1155
01:47:21,400 --> 01:47:24,559
..Yakup Bey and Melike Hatun..

1156
01:47:25,840 --> 01:47:30,879
..will surely cause trouble.
And we will do our move accordingly.

1157
01:47:31,880 --> 01:47:35,559
If the judge is here. So where is Orhan?

1158
01:47:36,240 --> 01:47:39,279
I hope he isn't in trouble. May Allah forbid that.

1159
01:47:42,440 --> 01:47:46,479
Well... That's what bothers me.

1160
01:47:46,880 --> 01:47:50,279
Now news from Orhan. I've sent alps after him.

1161
01:47:50,320 --> 01:47:52,839
I hope they won't attempt to harm him.

1162
01:47:52,920 --> 01:47:55,799
I hope they won't try to deceive
us in the trial...

1163
01:47:55,840 --> 01:47:59,039
...and put rope around my son's neck!

1164
01:47:59,480 --> 01:48:03,479
If they do, I'll
burn down the court over their heads!

1165
01:48:03,640 --> 01:48:07,039
You said there would be no weapons. How?

1166
01:48:07,440 --> 01:48:10,439
Aykurt! Turahan!

1167
01:48:26,880 --> 01:48:30,039
We have no swords, but...

1168
01:48:35,840 --> 01:48:38,799
...we have secret weapons...

1169
01:48:39,120 --> 01:48:41,999
...my Alaaddin Ali prepared.

1170
01:48:45,720 --> 01:48:47,479
Now...

1171
01:48:47,600 --> 01:48:49,479
Finish your preparations.

1172
01:48:49,640 --> 01:48:51,799
Be ready to fight.

1173
01:48:52,040 --> 01:48:54,119
As you order, my Bey.

1174
01:49:05,400 --> 01:49:08,399
Germiyanoglu Border - Frontier Market

1175
01:49:08,640 --> 01:49:11,319
Swords...

1176
01:49:11,640 --> 01:49:15,319
...will be hidden like this.

1177
01:49:23,480 --> 01:49:27,719
They will be put under
Germiyanoglu and Candaroglu like this.

1178
01:49:28,320 --> 01:49:33,919
I'll give these
to one of those on duty in the court.

1179
01:49:34,280 --> 01:49:37,439
And he'll place them in our section.

1180
01:49:39,840 --> 01:49:42,639
If a problem comes up

1181
01:49:43,040 --> 01:49:46,039
...we won’t be without weapons there.

1182
01:49:47,320 --> 01:49:50,159
A problem will come up, Mehmed Bey.

1183
01:49:50,360 --> 01:49:52,439
It will.

1184
01:49:52,720 --> 01:49:55,439
We'll turn the place into a bloodbath.

1185
01:49:55,640 --> 01:49:58,079
My son died.

1186
01:49:58,200 --> 01:50:02,399
Nothing but blood will cool off my heart.

1187
01:50:08,720 --> 01:50:12,159
Osman won't go there unprepared either.

1188
01:50:13,000 --> 01:50:20,359
For this reason, our alps
will wait somewhere close to the court.

1189
01:50:21,680 --> 01:50:25,879
And we'll be all prepared.

1190
01:50:39,160 --> 01:50:41,359
Why are you looking at me like that?

1191
01:50:41,520 --> 01:50:43,759
Don't be angry with me, Gonca.

1192
01:50:44,000 --> 01:50:46,679
I shouldn't be?

1193
01:50:47,160 --> 01:50:49,079
Why did you surrender, Alaaddin?

1194
01:50:49,200 --> 01:50:52,759
Don't you know what is going to happen?

1195
01:50:55,080 --> 01:50:56,879
What did I tell you, my hatun?

1196
01:50:56,960 --> 01:50:57,959
What?

1197
01:50:58,000 --> 01:51:01,919
I will never leave you alone.

1198
01:51:03,360 --> 01:51:05,559
I promised you.

1199
01:51:05,760 --> 01:51:08,359
I can't break my promise.

1200
01:51:09,280 --> 01:51:12,119
My Alaaddin, what if the judge doesn't believe us?

1201
01:51:12,160 --> 01:51:15,079
What will we do then?

1202
01:51:18,920 --> 01:51:21,479
We know the truth, Gonca.

1203
01:51:22,240 --> 01:51:25,159
I didn't kill Ahmed.

1204
01:51:28,360 --> 01:51:30,759
I don't know..

1205
01:51:30,840 --> 01:51:33,439
...if you killed him or not, but...

1206
01:51:33,640 --> 01:51:35,399
I'll kill you, Alaaddin.

1207
01:51:35,840 --> 01:51:40,199
-Brother, stop! Don't do this!
-Well...

1208
01:51:40,640 --> 01:51:43,079
That would suit you, Mehmed.

1209
01:51:43,280 --> 01:51:45,879
You tied me up. Come.

1210
01:51:46,080 --> 01:51:48,039
This is how you can only kill me.

1211
01:51:48,160 --> 01:51:50,479
You are a dead man, Alaaddin.

1212
01:51:50,880 --> 01:51:52,839
I don't hear you.

1213
01:51:53,760 --> 01:51:55,479
Brother, stop! Stop

1214
01:51:55,480 --> 01:51:57,439
-Get off!
-Brother, please stop!

1215
01:51:57,480 --> 01:52:01,079
That's enough!
Please stop! Enough!

1216
01:52:01,080 --> 01:52:02,959
Not enough!

1217
01:52:03,040 --> 01:52:04,799
Not enough.

1218
01:52:05,400 --> 01:52:07,239
You disrespected us.

1219
01:52:07,400 --> 01:52:10,999
-Our honor...
-Shut up! We didn't do anything.

1220
01:52:12,640 --> 01:52:15,519
I tried to talk to you many times.

1221
01:52:16,000 --> 01:52:18,799
But you never listened, Mehmed.

1222
01:52:19,200 --> 01:52:21,599
I said I loved your sister.

1223
01:52:21,800 --> 01:52:23,879
I said I fell in love.

1224
01:52:24,160 --> 01:52:27,559
And you? What did you do?

1225
01:52:30,720 --> 01:52:32,999
I believe..

1226
01:52:33,360 --> 01:52:35,999
...neither you nor your love, Alaaddin.

1227
01:52:36,160 --> 01:52:39,239
You did this to prevent our alliance with Candar.

1228
01:52:39,560 --> 01:52:41,479
You can’t protect mysister.

1229
01:52:43,240 --> 01:52:47,199
Brother, stop! For Allah's sake! Please stop!

1230
01:52:49,600 --> 01:52:52,159
You took my sister from me.

1231
01:52:52,440 --> 01:52:55,399
My sister no longer trusts me.

1232
01:52:56,080 --> 01:52:58,599
You've left me without a sister, Alaaddin.

1233
01:52:58,720 --> 01:53:01,079
You did this, Mehmed.

1234
01:53:01,800 --> 01:53:04,119
You should have acted like a brother...

1235
01:53:04,240 --> 01:53:06,319
...and supported us.

1236
01:53:07,400 --> 01:53:11,639
Brother, please stop! Don't do this! Don't!

1237
01:53:11,720 --> 01:53:14,399
Please, don't! Please stop!

1238
01:53:14,480 --> 01:53:17,399
You aren't a man who deserves to be supported!

1239
01:53:17,960 --> 01:53:20,799
You have to divorce my sister, Alaaddin!

1240
01:53:21,480 --> 01:53:24,519
You have to divorce my sister before you die!

1241
01:53:25,200 --> 01:53:29,679
Brother, please stop Please stop! Please!

1242
01:53:29,720 --> 01:53:32,599
Please! Leave him!

1243
01:53:33,480 --> 01:53:35,599
Please stop!

1244
01:53:38,840 --> 01:53:41,239
I'm not like you, Mehmed.

1245
01:53:41,720 --> 01:53:44,239
I'd do anything for my love.

1246
01:53:44,520 --> 01:53:47,319
I'd rather die than break my promise.

1247
01:53:47,360 --> 01:53:51,599
Please stop! You are mad! Please!

1248
01:53:51,600 --> 01:53:58,359
Brother, please stop!
Don't do this! Stop! You are mad! Stop!

1249
01:53:58,440 --> 01:54:02,399
-That's enough! Brother, please stop!
-Mehmed!

1250
01:54:02,400 --> 01:54:05,279
-Brother, stop! Stop!
-Leave him!

1251
01:54:05,280 --> 01:54:08,599
I won’t stop, father! I'm going to kill him!

1252
01:54:10,160 --> 01:54:12,159
I said stop.

1253
01:54:19,840 --> 01:54:23,639
They got Ibrahim Bey.

1254
01:54:25,040 --> 01:54:27,599
If this man dies

1255
01:54:28,560 --> 01:54:31,319
...Osman won't let him live.

1256
01:54:39,560 --> 01:54:41,759
You should be patient.

1257
01:54:43,040 --> 01:54:45,999
They're going to...

1258
01:54:47,200 --> 01:54:49,399
...be punished tomorrow, anyway.

1259
01:54:49,560 --> 01:54:52,679
Come on. Get out.

1260
01:55:15,240 --> 01:55:18,119
Alaaddin, are you alright?

1261
01:55:21,320 --> 01:55:23,279
I'm fine, Gonca.

1262
01:55:23,320 --> 01:55:25,239
I'm fine, my love.

1263
01:55:26,680 --> 01:55:29,599
I'm used to Mehmed's fists.

1264
01:55:29,880 --> 01:55:33,879
-Does it hurt?
-No, my love. It doesn't.

1265
01:55:54,680 --> 01:55:57,799
Alps! Sisters!

1266
01:55:57,880 --> 01:56:01,239
Today, we will
establish a court for Shahzade Alaeddin.

1267
01:56:01,440 --> 01:56:04,239
We will always stand by justice.

1268
01:56:04,360 --> 01:56:07,039
But... if we have to fight...

1269
01:56:07,160 --> 01:56:09,679
...at the end of the trial...

1270
01:56:09,760 --> 01:56:11,239
...we will fight.

1271
01:56:11,520 --> 01:56:16,479
Therefore, all of you will be ready.

1272
01:56:17,600 --> 01:56:19,999
When we give you the sign..

1273
01:56:20,560 --> 01:56:23,919
...your secret weapons will be revealed.

1274
01:56:47,040 --> 01:56:48,919
Come on!

1275
01:56:51,360 --> 01:56:55,359
Osman Bey said it... He
said "brothers' blood should not be shed"

1276
01:56:55,560 --> 01:56:59,719
But they are framing Tall Shahzade.

1277
01:57:00,000 --> 01:57:04,359
Why would Muslims
do this to each other to shed blood?

1278
01:57:04,680 --> 01:57:08,239
Because they fall for the shaytaan's games.

1279
01:57:08,360 --> 01:57:12,079
He has such treacherous traps that...

1280
01:57:12,440 --> 01:57:16,519
...nafs makes you companions with shaytaan.

1281
01:57:16,600 --> 01:57:18,679
What are those traps?

1282
01:57:18,840 --> 01:57:23,159
You are the Sultan of words. You will
tell me, right?

1283
01:57:23,200 --> 01:57:25,639
Cowardice...

1284
01:57:25,880 --> 01:57:28,759
...considering yourself superior...

1285
01:57:28,920 --> 01:57:33,159
...the desire for power, fame, and glory...

1286
01:57:33,800 --> 01:57:37,279
...greed, sacrificing everything...

1287
01:57:37,600 --> 01:57:40,519
...for gold...

1288
01:57:40,680 --> 01:57:44,319
...serving the servants for properties...

1289
01:57:44,760 --> 01:57:48,639
Shaytaan has other traps, but...

1290
01:57:48,720 --> 01:57:52,199
...there is one trap...

1291
01:57:52,520 --> 01:57:56,119
...that is arrogance.

1292
01:57:56,600 --> 01:57:59,719
The love of self.

1293
01:57:59,880 --> 01:58:03,239
Thinking you deserve everything.

1294
01:58:03,600 --> 01:58:06,199
The Muslim who falls into that trap...

1295
01:58:06,320 --> 01:58:09,759
...walks with arrogance.

1296
01:58:09,840 --> 01:58:12,519
He slanders his brother...

1297
01:58:12,640 --> 01:58:14,759
...sheds his blood...

1298
01:58:14,840 --> 01:58:18,039
..and thinks he is right.

1299
01:58:18,080 --> 01:58:20,519
Like Cain.

1300
01:58:20,600 --> 01:58:22,639
Do you know Cain and Abel?

1301
01:58:22,720 --> 01:58:23,839
I do...

1302
01:58:23,880 --> 01:58:27,039
...but we are not Cain, right?

1303
01:58:27,120 --> 01:58:31,519
Not my Osman Bey. But are they Cain?

1304
01:58:31,600 --> 01:58:34,679
The slanderers?

1305
01:58:34,840 --> 01:58:39,599
We don't know who is Cain and who is Abel for sure.

1306
01:58:39,760 --> 01:58:41,839
But what we know is that...

1307
01:58:42,000 --> 01:58:44,919
...Osman Bey seeks peace to...

1308
01:58:45,080 --> 01:58:47,239
...avoid shedding brotherly blood.

1309
01:58:47,360 --> 01:58:49,559
He does not leave the true path...

1310
01:58:49,760 --> 01:58:53,519
...he does not fall into the traps of shaytaan.

1311
01:58:53,640 --> 01:58:55,919
Therefore...

1312
01:58:55,960 --> 01:59:00,279
...if there is anyone
to spread Islam's da'wah to the world...

1313
01:59:01,160 --> 01:59:04,079
...it is surely him.

1314
01:59:10,200 --> 01:59:11,679
Osman Bey...

1315
01:59:25,920 --> 01:59:28,559
Ibrahim Bey.

1316
01:59:28,920 --> 01:59:32,559
Today, justice will be established.

1317
01:59:36,640 --> 01:59:39,879
You speak of justice to a man...

1318
01:59:40,440 --> 01:59:43,039
...you unjustly took as a captive.

1319
01:59:43,200 --> 01:59:47,159
I don't believe a word you say, Osman Bey!

1320
01:59:47,440 --> 01:59:50,839
Is that so?

1321
01:59:51,640 --> 01:59:54,879
Will you not be
persuaded even by what the judge says?

1322
01:59:54,960 --> 01:59:56,799
Ha?

1323
01:59:56,920 --> 01:59:59,159
Despite him...

1324
01:59:59,200 --> 02:00:01,519
Will you still try to kill my son?

1325
02:00:01,600 --> 02:00:04,399
If your son...

1326
02:00:04,480 --> 02:00:08,599
...had not made a move, none of this
would have happened.

1327
02:00:12,480 --> 02:00:16,119
Ibrahim Bey is poisoned with hatred.

1328
02:00:16,880 --> 02:00:19,439
He blames others...

1329
02:00:19,480 --> 02:00:22,719
...he never blames himself.

1330
02:00:22,800 --> 02:00:23,479
But...

1331
02:00:25,240 --> 02:00:27,879
...those like him...

1332
02:00:28,800 --> 02:00:31,999
...only hurt themselves.

1333
02:00:32,440 --> 02:00:34,359
Release his hands.

1334
02:00:34,560 --> 02:00:37,479
There's no need to tie his hands.

1335
02:00:38,560 --> 02:00:42,639
Come on. Take him.

1336
02:01:04,160 --> 02:01:06,599
O people...

1337
02:01:06,600 --> 02:01:11,519
The court that will happen today
might turn into a battlefield anytime!

1338
02:01:11,680 --> 02:01:17,119
Everyone will be ready!
Everyone will be ready for a battle!

1339
02:01:26,360 --> 02:01:29,279
Come on!

1340
02:02:04,720 --> 02:02:07,999
My Shahzade...

1341
02:02:09,520 --> 02:02:12,639
Holofira... Are you alright?

1342
02:02:13,400 --> 02:02:17,199
Come on! Put him in the cart!

1343
02:02:54,360 --> 02:02:57,559
These are your last breaths.

1344
02:02:57,880 --> 02:03:00,399
Take a deep one.

1345
02:03:00,640 --> 02:03:03,199
Melike Hatun.

1346
02:03:03,360 --> 02:03:06,559
We must not delay justice.

1347
02:03:06,800 --> 02:03:09,879
Let the truth be exposed.

1348
02:03:10,040 --> 02:03:14,359
Those involved will be punished.

1349
02:03:24,440 --> 02:03:26,679
It is time.

1350
02:04:05,000 --> 02:04:09,319
Your poor fear won’t delay your death.

1351
02:04:09,600 --> 02:04:13,719
Don't you trust the great
justice? Why did you gather here like mice?

1352
02:04:14,760 --> 02:04:17,199
We trust justice...

1353
02:04:17,240 --> 02:04:20,319
...but we do not trust your dastardness!

1354
02:04:23,480 --> 02:04:25,919
If you do not trust great justice...

1355
02:04:26,000 --> 02:04:29,079
...just as we got under the soil before death...

1356
02:04:29,080 --> 02:04:32,199
...we know how to rain from the holy sky.

1357
02:04:32,280 --> 02:04:36,879
I will bring the sky down upon you Olcay!

1358
02:04:41,640 --> 02:04:44,959
I stand before you with an army that loves death...

1359
02:04:45,040 --> 02:04:48,359
...as much as you love life!

1360
02:04:48,640 --> 02:04:52,119
Now get lost or I'll crush you!

1361
02:04:52,920 --> 02:04:55,079
You escaped from me once.

1362
02:04:55,720 --> 02:04:58,559
But there won't be a second time, Gunduz.

1363
02:04:59,160 --> 02:05:01,919
The skies above will also determine your fate.

1364
02:05:03,040 --> 02:05:06,359
He is still talking, get lost!

1365
02:05:28,000 --> 02:05:30,119
Is everything ready, Yakup Bey?

1366
02:05:30,160 --> 02:05:33,559
We are sitting on our swords.

1367
02:05:56,080 --> 02:05:59,839
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

1368
02:06:15,840 --> 02:06:18,279
Sit down.

1369
02:06:26,840 --> 02:06:29,959
On the 10th day of Shawwal...

1370
02:06:30,080 --> 02:06:33,399
...the trial for the accusation of Osman
Bey's son Alaeddin...

1371
02:06:33,520 --> 02:06:35,839
...murdering the son of Ibrahim Bey...

1372
02:06:35,920 --> 02:06:39,759
...from the Candar tribe, Ahmed Bey...

1373
02:06:40,120 --> 02:06:42,639
...has begun.

1374
02:06:54,760 --> 02:06:57,879
On the day Ahmed Bey was killed...

1375
02:06:57,880 --> 02:07:00,279
...you were in that tent to abduct Gonca Hatun...

1376
02:07:00,400 --> 02:07:03,159
...right, Alaeddin Bey?

1377
02:07:03,480 --> 02:07:06,199
Yes, dear judge

1378
02:07:06,760 --> 02:07:09,079
-But I did not kill..
-Do not answer...

1379
02:07:09,120 --> 02:07:13,479
...before you are asked to speak, Alaeddin Bey.

1380
02:07:13,640 --> 02:07:16,199
Did Ahmed Bey resist you...

1381
02:07:16,320 --> 02:07:19,479
...or a fight happen between you?

1382
02:07:19,880 --> 02:07:22,319
Yes, dear judge

1383
02:07:22,400 --> 02:07:25,599
And you are still claiming that you did
not kill Ahmed Bey.

1384
02:07:25,600 --> 02:07:28,199
Do you know where you stabbed the dagger?

1385
02:07:28,360 --> 02:07:30,839
It was Ahmed Bey who drew his dagger.

1386
02:07:31,040 --> 02:07:33,039
I did not touch my dagger.

1387
02:07:33,080 --> 02:07:38,199
Could you... fight my
son when he was holding a dagger?

1388
02:07:38,920 --> 02:07:40,799
He is lying, dear judge.

1389
02:07:40,800 --> 02:07:44,639
Ibrahim Bey,
do not speak before I ask you to speak.

1390
02:07:49,080 --> 02:07:51,759
I was not alone there, dear judge.

1391
02:07:51,800 --> 02:07:57,119
Dear judge... We want you to hear the witnesses.

1392
02:07:57,200 --> 02:08:00,639
Gonca... and Holofira.

1393
02:08:02,040 --> 02:08:03,639
They were there.

1394
02:08:03,720 --> 02:08:05,399
Gonca Hatun.

1395
02:08:05,520 --> 02:08:08,719
Holofira Hatun. Come forward.

1396
02:08:18,160 --> 02:08:20,879
Are they going to be your witnesses, Osman Bey?

1397
02:08:21,320 --> 02:08:24,279
One of them is the
Hatun of the accused Alaeddin Bey...

1398
02:08:24,360 --> 02:08:27,719
...the other is
a Christian who is living with your people.

1399
02:08:28,120 --> 02:08:31,479
Besides, both are women!

1400
02:08:32,040 --> 02:08:35,919
Their testimonies are invalid.

1401
02:08:41,960 --> 02:08:43,959
It is not enough!

1402
02:08:44,240 --> 02:08:48,759
These two Hatuns are also the accomplices.

1403
02:08:50,160 --> 02:08:55,439
If the guilt is proven,
they will be sentenced like Alaeddin Bey.

1404
02:09:01,960 --> 02:09:06,079
Dear judge.. What are you saying?

1405
02:09:06,320 --> 02:09:10,079
You're saying our witnesses'...

1406
02:09:10,600 --> 02:09:13,879
...testimonies are invalid for our innocence...

1407
02:09:14,240 --> 02:09:17,479
...and that our evidence is insufficient.

1408
02:09:23,080 --> 02:09:25,999
Then tell me

1409
02:09:27,520 --> 02:09:32,279
Show me the
evidence that proves Alaeddin killed Ahmed!

1410
02:09:45,520 --> 02:09:48,919
We'll be there soon, come on!

1411
02:09:57,280 --> 02:10:00,679
Just to blame us...

1412
02:10:01,240 --> 02:10:06,199
You're doing this so that we turn
against each other when Alaeddin is out.

1413
02:10:06,680 --> 02:10:08,839
Now tell me.

1414
02:10:09,160 --> 02:10:12,679
Show me the proof
that Ahmed was not killed by someone else.

1415
02:10:12,680 --> 02:10:15,039
While there are many suspects

1416
02:10:15,120 --> 02:10:17,799
you're talking about a murderer that doesn't exist.

1417
02:10:17,920 --> 02:10:20,359
You're diverting the court from its purpose.

1418
02:10:20,440 --> 02:10:22,799
This is not the place to talk about theories,

1419
02:10:22,800 --> 02:10:24,959
but it is the place to talk about truth.

1420
02:10:25,040 --> 02:10:30,839
What if our theory is more true than your verdict?

1421
02:10:31,040 --> 02:10:33,879
Then...

1422
02:10:34,080 --> 02:10:38,079
...you will show the
proof that Alaeddin killed Ahmed Bey.

1423
02:10:38,400 --> 02:10:42,839
We are the servants of justice, we exist for this.

1424
02:10:43,120 --> 02:10:46,839
When the proof is not enough

1425
02:10:47,080 --> 02:10:49,199
we make the verdict.

1426
02:10:49,440 --> 02:10:53,279
If everything was clear, we wouldn't be needed.

1427
02:10:55,800 --> 02:11:00,079
Before I tell my verdict, I'd like to hear

1428
02:11:00,240 --> 02:11:02,799
last defense of Alaeddin Bey.

1429
02:11:05,240 --> 02:11:08,759
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

1430
02:11:10,240 --> 02:11:14,799
"Then they are all returned to Allah

1431
02:11:14,920 --> 02:11:18,639
their True Master.

1432
02:11:18,760 --> 02:11:22,719
Judgment is His.

1433
02:11:22,920 --> 02:11:25,519
And He is the...

1434
02:11:25,600 --> 02:11:27,919
...Swiftest Reckoner."
[Surah Al-An'am - 62]

1435
02:11:28,600 --> 02:11:31,319
You are distorting The Creator's justice.

1436
02:11:31,440 --> 02:11:34,679
Show a precedent for such a verdict.

1437
02:11:35,400 --> 02:11:38,399
Your punishment will be heavy,
dear judge.

1438
02:11:38,720 --> 02:11:40,799
But don't worry.

1439
02:11:40,960 --> 02:11:44,359
My Creator is the Swiftest Reckoner.

1440
02:11:44,680 --> 02:11:49,239
-Don't you forget.
-All the signs lead to you, Alaeddin Bey.

1441
02:11:49,400 --> 02:11:52,279
Isn't Gonca your Hatun?

1442
02:11:52,360 --> 02:11:56,359
Wasn't Ahmed Bey your rival?

1443
02:11:56,920 --> 02:11:58,919
You were the first one to question...

1444
02:11:59,040 --> 02:12:01,439
...even if you weren't there.

1445
02:12:01,720 --> 02:12:04,479
Such a verdict was inevitable.

1446
02:12:11,880 --> 02:12:16,359
Since everything is clear, it is time for verdict.

1447
02:12:20,600 --> 02:12:24,319
First of all, I will give
the verdict of the so-called witnesses.

1448
02:12:24,520 --> 02:12:26,319
Holofira Hatun.

1449
02:12:26,320 --> 02:12:31,919
She will be banished and she will not
come to the lands of any of the Beyliks.

1450
02:12:33,520 --> 02:12:37,879
Gonca Hatun will be spared.

1451
02:12:37,880 --> 02:12:40,479
She will be given back to her household.

1452
02:12:42,040 --> 02:12:47,359
-And the marriage will be over.
-What are you talking about, dear judge?

1453
02:12:47,920 --> 02:12:51,679
This is not justice, this is not the right verdict!

1454
02:12:52,760 --> 02:12:55,199
You even captured us

1455
02:12:55,240 --> 02:12:58,239
saying that the court will be set up.

1456
02:12:58,560 --> 02:13:02,399
And now, are you going to go against the

1457
02:13:02,440 --> 02:13:05,719
The judge's verdict?

1458
02:13:22,480 --> 02:13:26,559
May Allah protect us
from shedding the blood of our brothers.

1459
02:13:26,640 --> 02:13:28,719
Gunduz Bey!

1460
02:13:28,760 --> 02:13:31,159
Infidels want this from us.

1461
02:13:31,200 --> 02:13:35,679
But we will never give them what they want.

1462
02:13:36,040 --> 02:13:38,319
Thank Allah.

1463
02:13:38,360 --> 02:13:40,119
Right.

1464
02:13:40,240 --> 02:13:43,199
Right, but let's be prepared.

1465
02:13:50,120 --> 02:13:52,479
Tell us your verdict, dear judge.

1466
02:13:52,680 --> 02:13:54,519
Alaeddin Bey...

1467
02:13:54,560 --> 02:13:59,839
...was found guilty of
the murder of Candaroglu Ahmed Bey.

1468
02:14:07,440 --> 02:14:09,439
Thankfully.

1469
02:14:09,520 --> 02:14:11,759
There's life in retaliation.

1470
02:14:11,800 --> 02:14:16,959
That is why, Alaeddin Bey will be executed.

1471
02:14:18,160 --> 02:14:22,119
No, son. Alaeddin, no.

1472
02:14:22,480 --> 02:14:24,279
Dear judge.

1473
02:14:24,400 --> 02:14:27,359
When you don't have any proof

1474
02:14:27,360 --> 02:14:30,079
how can you convict the innocent?

1475
02:14:30,360 --> 02:14:32,599
Osman, Osman.

1476
02:14:32,760 --> 02:14:35,599
They are going to hang our son.

1477
02:14:37,480 --> 02:14:41,799
-Alaeddin!
-Gonca!

1478
02:14:44,000 --> 02:14:47,719
-Mehmed!
-Let go off me. Alaeddin!

1479
02:14:48,000 --> 02:14:50,759
Let go off me! Alaeddin!

1480
02:14:50,880 --> 02:14:54,679
Let go off me! Let go off me!

1481
02:14:54,840 --> 02:14:58,399
Let me go! Alaeddin!

1482
02:14:58,480 --> 02:15:04,039
Alaeddin! Osman Bey!
Alaeddin! I said let him go!

1483
02:15:04,120 --> 02:15:08,319
Alaeddin! No! No!

1484
02:15:08,400 --> 02:15:11,039
Let him go!

1485
02:15:11,160 --> 02:15:15,599
Let go off him! Alaeddin! Alaeddin!

1486
02:15:15,680 --> 02:15:21,279
No! No! Alaeddin! Let him go!

1487
02:15:24,040 --> 02:15:25,839
Stop!

1488
02:15:27,960 --> 02:15:29,039
Brother.

1489
02:15:29,160 --> 02:15:32,119
This judge is fake!

1490
02:15:36,480 --> 02:15:40,319
They killed the true judge, Rukneddin.

1491
02:15:53,000 --> 02:15:56,839
Would you do this to distort justice, Osman Bey?

1492
02:15:57,200 --> 02:16:00,079
Shut up!

1493
02:16:09,520 --> 02:16:13,439
So you're here with your swords?

1494
02:16:20,160 --> 02:16:23,079
Show the letter that Osman Bey invited you.

1495
02:16:23,360 --> 02:16:26,879
-You are setting me up!
-They are lying!

1496
02:16:27,440 --> 02:16:30,639
They are lying to save their murderer son!

1497
02:16:30,720 --> 02:16:33,239
Is that so?

1498
02:16:34,600 --> 02:16:37,279
Look at me.

1499
02:16:39,160 --> 02:16:40,718
This is the plan of Kayis!

1500
02:16:40,879 --> 02:16:45,439
Is this your justice? Move away!

1501
02:16:49,200 --> 02:16:51,999
Is this your justice?

1502
02:16:52,240 --> 02:16:54,839
Justice?

1503
02:16:54,879 --> 02:16:58,398
Justice.

1504
02:16:58,680 --> 02:17:00,839
Is this your justice?

1505
02:17:00,840 --> 02:17:04,039
Is it?

1506
02:17:05,280 --> 02:17:10,239
You'd kill my son with a fake judge, is that so?

1507
02:17:14,719 --> 02:17:19,159
You came with
your swords to kill us all, is that so?

1508
02:17:19,680 --> 02:17:20,599
Is that so?

1509
02:17:20,639 --> 02:17:23,039
There's no such thing, Osman Bey!

1510
02:17:23,440 --> 02:17:27,478
We didn't know that judge was fake.

1511
02:17:27,480 --> 02:17:29,279
What about you?

1512
02:17:29,600 --> 02:17:32,999
You hid sword inside of the banner.

1513
02:17:33,080 --> 02:17:36,439
No matter how many traps the hunter sets,

1514
02:17:36,558 --> 02:17:41,159
the wolf finds a way.

1515
02:17:41,320 --> 02:17:43,839
You were going to kill us.

1516
02:17:44,000 --> 02:17:47,279
You were going to kill my son.

1517
02:17:48,080 --> 02:17:49,638
Do you think I'd just watch?

1518
02:17:49,680 --> 02:17:52,398
Justice doesn't hurt, you're wrong!

1519
02:17:52,400 --> 02:17:54,879
Shut up! Shut up!

1520
02:17:55,000 --> 02:17:59,558
You're still talking.
You're still talking.

1521
02:18:02,879 --> 02:18:05,439
Ibrahim Bey. Ibrahim Bey.

1522
02:18:05,480 --> 02:18:09,638
They are killing the judge in front of us.
Do something.

1523
02:18:09,719 --> 02:18:13,478
How have we survived this long?

1524
02:18:14,200 --> 02:18:17,279
With justice.

1525
02:18:17,719 --> 02:18:20,558
By ruling with justice.

1526
02:18:21,320 --> 02:18:26,239
But if injustice gets inside,

1527
02:18:26,360 --> 02:18:29,519
then peace will be gone in the nation.

1528
02:18:29,558 --> 02:18:34,478
I will not let anyone use justice for revenge.

1529
02:18:34,600 --> 02:18:38,999
I will not let anyone use justice for their
evil purposes!

1530
02:18:39,080 --> 02:18:42,318
How dare you talk like this?

1531
02:18:42,558 --> 02:18:44,239
Are you the State?

1532
02:18:44,320 --> 02:18:46,679
Everywhere I set foot

1533
02:18:46,799 --> 02:18:50,079
I'm the Bey, and I'm the State.

1534
02:18:50,120 --> 02:18:53,119
Come here.

1535
02:19:23,040 --> 02:19:25,999
As long as there are dastards like him,

1536
02:19:26,120 --> 02:19:30,919
as long as there are
those who make plans behind our back

1537
02:19:31,040 --> 02:19:33,318
from now

1538
02:19:33,320 --> 02:19:34,558
from now on,

1539
02:19:35,680 --> 02:19:37,519
I'm the justice.

1540
02:19:47,205 --> 02:20:01,125
Visit turkision.com for more!